like a sonic boom. Yukiko woke one night, bathed in cold sweat, to the piercing shrieks of her neighbor’s child. Rushing outside, she witnessed a scene that froze her blood.\n\nA bioluminescent beast, unlike anything she’d ever seen, stalked through the colony’s streets. Its carapace, the color of molten lava, pulsed with an inner light. Its limbs, tipped with razor-sharp claws, ripped through the bio-walls with ease. Strapped to the creature were canisters, emblazoned with the words I AM across the side. People, screaming, scattered like startled birds.\n\nThe sight of her mother and brother, cowering behind a fallen tree, their faces etched with terror, spurred Yukiko into action. Grabbing a discarded bio-tool, she charged towards the monster, a tiny David to its Goliath. Her attack was desperate, fueled by fear and a primal need to protect. The creature, seemingly surprised by her audacity, turned its luminous eyes towards her. For a heart-stopping moment, it held her gaze, then, with a guttural screech, it leaped over her, vanishing into the alien night.\n\nExhausted, shaking, Yukiko fell to her knees. The colony, once a gleaming oasis in the unknown, lay in ruins around her. Her decision, made in a moment of panic, had unleashed a nightmare upon them. Beneath the terror, a spark of defiance flickered. The silence of the ERB, she realized, had not cut them off from Earth. It had severed the only thing that was holding the unnatural world around them at bay.\n\nThe dawn of another Sorhhinda day arrived, but the colony it bathed in bore the scars of the previous night. Ruins smoldered, bio-tech lay mangled, and the air thrummed with a raw, primal dread. Even amidst the wreckage, embers of hope flickered.\n\nYukiko, the inadvertent architect of this new reality, stood amongst the survivors, her small hand tightly clasping her mother’s. As Governor Tanaka’s booming voice rallied the colonists, Yukiko felt a knot of guilt loosen in her chest. This wasn’t her burden a