man before me to hold their breath. Then I answered, my voice like iron.\n\n“They fight for control,” I said. “We fight for survival. They wield dreams for domination—we shape them for preservation. They think they can bend this realm to their will. They don’t realize we’re here to burn it down.”\n\nA rumble of approval spread through the ranks, the exhaustion cracking under the weight of something stronger—purpose.\n\nThen the veteran spoke, his voice like gravel grinding against steel. “What’s the next move, Commander?”\n\nI met his gaze. The next move was the only one left.\n\n“We strike at their core,” I said, my voice cutting through the night. “Deep in the realm of nightmares lies their stronghold. No gods, no prayers—just horrors beyond imagining.” I let the silence stretch, then drove the nail home. “We go there. We face them. And we remind them why we are not to be fucking trifled with.”\n\nAnother ripple, this time sharper. A spark catching dry tinder. The shift from weariness to readiness.	83	ai_extracted	2026-02-27 12:11:27.804895-05	2026-03-05 19:39:33.692739-05	\N	17	\N	\N
