owards a purpose that aligns with the collective march of humanity towards the stars.\n\n“Back to the fucking grindstone.” I think to myself as I begin the torture that is the task of updating my resume.\n\nAs Lysteria’s space ring crests the horizon, humanity’s journey diverges from the boundless wanderings of the dreamscape. Here, we do not drift through illusion, but carve our path through the marrow of reality itself—where the thrill is not in the unknown, but in the undeniable, the touchable, the real. Although the universe may stretch out before us, vast and mysterious, it is here, within the joys and challenges of everyday life on Earth, that we find our own unique allure, even with all the pain, suffering and disgust we face on a daily basis.\n\nI sit there and think to myself, I really should write a book about all these dreams and profound shit I think about. But then the idea passes, a fleeting memory soon to be forgotten.\n\n“An author. Yeah right.” I mutter to myself. “Dreams come to Earth to fucking die.”	88	ai_extracted	2026-02-27 12:12:25.367353-05	2026-03-05 19:39:33.692739-05	\N	18	\N	\N
