re filter over reality and called it architecture. Above us, lines of code continue streaming: CONTAINMENT PROTOCOL ACTIVE, SUBJECTS SECURED, PROCESSING INITIATED.\n\n"Where are we?" Becca asks, her artist's eye taking in details even while paralyzed. "This place doesn't follow any rules. The perspective is all wrong."\n\nThat's when the Auditor appears.\n\nHe doesn't walk in—he just is, suddenly sitting behind a desk that materialized while we weren't looking. The thing defies description in the same way the void outside defied color. An undulating pillar of infinite frequencies contained within the illusion of a plain man in a beige suit that shifts textures when observed. Sometimes wool, sometimes silk, sometimes scales or static electricity.\n\n"Subjects," he says, and his voice resonates through our bones like tuning forks. "You have been brought here for evaluation regarding recent violations of established protocols."\n\n"Violations?" I try to shake my head but can't. "What the hell are you talking about?"\n\nJamie's breathing becomes rapid and shallow beside me. I can see her in my peripheral vision, her skin starting to glow with that inner light I've come to recognize. "Stephen," she whispers, and there's pure terror in her voice. "They're going to separate us. They're going to reset me back to what I was before."\n\n"Subject Velistra," the Auditor interrupts, consulting a file that wasn't there a moment ago. "Status: Compromised Asset. Emotional attachment to Target Glitch has resulted in mission failure."\n\n"You won't separate us!" Jamie screams, and suddenly she's not Jamie anymore—she's something else entirely. Her skin erupts in flames that burn without heat, her bones crack and stretch, elongating her limbs. "I am ME! Velistra AND Jamie! We chose to merge!"\n\nThe restraints around her wrists don't just crack—they explode into molten fragments. Her fingers extend into razor-sharp talons dripping with something that might be acid or liquid starlight.