5	Yaldabaoth Variant — The Demiurge Shard [Class A]	t	A true fragment of Yaldabaoth's divine power, broken off and operating with semi-autonomous purpose. It manifests as a writhing mass of mouths and eyes encased in a cracked shell of corrupted golden light — like a piece of a shattered god still trying to function as the whole. Each mouth speaks in a different language simultaneously. Each eye focuses on a different dimension. The shell pulses and fractures continuously, leaking tendrils of liquid shadow that reach for anything living. Where it floats, reality develops hairline cracks — fine as spider silk, spreading outward in geometric patterns. It is unmistakably a piece of something unimaginably larger, and that implication is perhaps more terrifying than the shard itself.	Fractured megalomania. Each mouth expresses a different facet of Yaldabaoth's personality simultaneously — one rages, one bargains, one weeps, one commands, one simply screams. The overall effect is a cacophony of divine narcissism struggling to maintain coherence without the whole.	A dissonant chord of multiple voices speaking over each other in dead and living languages. The wet sound of mouths opening and closing. A crystalline ringing when its shell fractures further. Beneath it all, a deep, tectonic groan — the sound of broken divinity.	Burnt sugar and formaldehyde. The cloying, overripe sweetness of divinity left to rot, mixed with the sharp preservative tang of something trying desperately not to decay further.	Encased in a cracked shell of corrupted divine light that serves as both armor and containment. Fragments of the shell can be weaponized as projectile shrapnel.	Localized reality manipulation — can warp physics, reverse causality, and unmake matter within a limited radius. Each mouth can cast independently, creating overlapping fields of hostile effect. The eyes can lock onto targets across dimensional boundaries, making conventional hiding impossible. When damaged, it sheds shell fragments that continue to function as autonomous hazards. Can temporarily merge with the local environment, making walls speak and floors hunger.	When Yaldabaoth was weakened or wounded across the cycles of its imprisonment, pieces broke away. Each shard retains a portion of the Demiurge's power and personality but lacks the unified will that makes the whole so dangerous. They are, in a sense, feral gods — divine power without divine purpose, running on fragmented instinct.	"I AM I AM I AM I AM I AM — which one of me is speaking? Does it matter? Every mouth is mine. Every word is law. KNEEL."	Class A — the first variant that wields genuine divine power rather than psychological tricks or environmental control. A Demiurge Shard is a legitimate existential threat within its radius of influence. However, its fractured nature is both its strength (unpredictable, multi-vector attacks) and its weakness (it cannot coordinate its many selves effectively, creating openings between its conflicting impulses).	\N	anthropic	claude-opus-4-6	2026-03-01 14:37:14.948981-05	2026-03-14 18:06:15.112419-04	2	\N
