46	The Pointers (Collective Entity)	t	Silent, eternally still figures with vacant stares pointing skyward; their unified presence creates an aura of incomprehensible transcendence. They materialize unexpectedly in public spaces, their absolute silence and stillness generating gravitational pull of attention across global society. Their forms are characterized by complete immobility and enigmatic purpose, radiating a quality that resists all attempts at rational explanation.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	They 'materialized like urban mirages in bustling plazas and sun-drenched beaches, their silence a stark counterpoint to our ceaseless chatter.' The text notes their 'vacant stares and unmoving limbs' and that 'the world was transfixed, collectively holding its breath for the next sighting.' Their 'enigmatic presence had left a mark on society, making us question our own existence.'	The Pointers simply point skyward in absolute silence and stillness, their unmoving limbs and vacant stares creating a phenomenon that defies explanation and consumes the consciousness of observers. Their very presence asks the question: 'Were they prophets, performance artists, harbingers of the unknown?'	Unlike typical creatures or entities, The Pointers are defined by complete absence of action, communication, or change—their power lies entirely in their enigmatic stillness and the psychological/societal obsession they generate. They operate on a level beyond conventional threat; they are a mini-boss of consciousness itself, capable of consuming entire societies' attention and transforming how individuals understand reality.	3	claude	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	2026-02-27 12:58:50.898794-05	2026-03-14 18:06:15.112419-04	2	\N
