57	The Pointers (Celestial Manifestation)	t	A spectral collective entity appearing as multiple figures under sodium glow with faces etched in alien serenity, arms outstretched toward the infinite expanse above. They emanate an aura of mysterious spiritual energy, their stillness evoking both profound calm and existential dread. The air around them carries a cloying sweetness of bitter dreams, suggesting they exist at the threshold between waking and transcendent realms.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Described as a 'spectral tableau' standing with 'unwavering certainty'; their 'stillness' evokes both awe and terror in the narrator; they are the object of weeks-long obsessive search and the catalyst for the narrator's internal crisis of desire versus fear.	Standing motionless with arms outstretched toward 'the inky expanse above,' their stillness haunts the narrator long after escape: 'haunted by their stillness, their unwavering certainty.'	Unlike ordinary manifestations, The Pointers possess a tangible presence capable of inspiring profound spiritual yearning while simultaneously triggering primal fear. Their 'alien serenity' and apparent access to transcendent realms make them a unique threat—not through aggression, but through their power to destabilize the narrator's grasp on mundane reality and compel either transcendence or flight.	4	claude	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	2026-02-27 12:59:17.07896-05	2026-03-14 18:06:15.112419-04	2	\N
