69	The Enigmatic Pointers	t	A creature or collective entity with absolutely no documented history prior to their sudden appearance in the world. They exist as a complete mystery, surrounded by speculation and conspiracy theories. Their nature remains utterly undefined—whether they are supernatural beings, time travelers, failed government experiments, or something else entirely remains unknowable.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	No records of them ever existing before their sudden appearance. No one knows who they are or where they came from. They have captivated the narrator's mind despite remaining enigmatic. One theory claims they were part of a government experiment involving telepathic communication gone wrong, resulting in catatonia.	They remained an enigma, a mystery that refused to be solved.	Unlike typical enemies or creatures, The Pointers pose a threat through their absolute inscrutability rather than direct action. Their power lies in generating obsession, uncertainty, and the impossibility of understanding. They are a cognitive and psychological threat rather than a physical one—their very existence defies explanation and consumes the mind of anyone attempting to understand them.	5	claude	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	2026-02-27 12:59:41.749694-05	2026-03-14 18:06:15.112419-04	2	\N
