255	The Eternal Absence	t	A gnawing, inexorable emptiness that dwells at the core of the narrator's being; manifests as a persistent hollow that no achievement, power, or transformation can fill; more insidious than any external enemy because it cannot be conquered through will or understanding alone.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Despite achievements, the narrator confronts 'an aching void' that 'would always remain, a gnawing sense that something essential would always be missing.' This absence outlasts all other obstacles and becomes the primary antagonist of the narrator's inner journey.	No matter how much I would achieve, an aching void would always remain, a gnawing sense that something essential would always be missing. My screams for relief would always fall on deaf ears.	Unlike external enemies (church, parents, medics), the Eternal Absence cannot be defied, deceived, or defeated through rebellion. It grows stronger with achievement and persists despite mastery of inner realms. It is the true curse of the narrator's power—the price of transcendence.	15	claude	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	2026-02-27 13:13:14.35138-05	2026-03-14 18:06:15.112419-04	2	\N
