270	The Weight of Silence	t	A crushing, almost physical manifestation of social ostracism. It spreads across the space between the narrator and their friends like a toxic fog, visible in frozen faces and the shift from warmth to unease. Its presence is louder than any spoken rejection could ever be.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	"No one spoke. Their silence was louder than rejection, their discomfort a reminder that I was no longer one of the group, just another broken curiosity, a lost cause beyond repair." The weight of rejection hits harder than expected, demonstrating the mini-boss's power over physical and emotional resilience.	"No one spoke. Their silence was louder than rejection."	Unlike ordinary social rejection, The Weight of Silence is weaponized through absence—what is NOT said becomes more destructive than what could be said. It transforms friends into unwitting executioners of the narrator's hope.	16	claude	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	2026-02-27 13:14:09.015358-05	2026-03-14 18:06:15.112419-04	2	\N
