329	The Pulling Darkness	t	An invisible but palpable opposition that manifests as a force pulling the protagonist backward. It represents the fundamental resistance between dream and waking, between preservation and dissolution. Present as a pervasive weight throughout the protagonist's desperate flight.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Described as 'an unseen force pulling me back' and 'a battle against an unseen force pulling me back.' It compounds the claustrophobic weight of urgency and manifests most powerfully in Beat 2 as the protagonist races toward home.	The Pulling Darkness exerts constant, invisible resistance: 'each step a battle against an unseen force pulling me back.'	Unlike abstract manifestations of emotion, The Pulling Darkness is an active, adversarial force opposing the protagonist's every action. It is the primary antagonistic force of this scene—more dangerous than doubt or fear because it is entirely external and insurmountable, working in concert with the dissolution of dream elements to ensure failure.	20	claude	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	2026-02-27 13:16:09.683429-05	2026-03-14 18:06:15.112419-04	2	\N
