363	Board Members (Collective Gaslighting Entity)	t	A unified force of corporate executives embodying systemic indifference masked by performative celebration. Their collective silent judgment presses in like vultures; their irrelevant questions are precision strikes at composure; their final applause is a denial of visible reality. CEO Francine leads their choir of invalidation, her 'enlightening' comment becoming the moment composure shatters.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Silent judgment pressing in like vultures; barrage of irrelevant questions (Spider-Man colors, Fred's retirement, zoom functionality); CEO's muttered 'This is... enlightening' during software crash; faux-concern question about testing; final standing ovation and handshake despite visible failures.	CEO Francine leans back and mutters: 'This is... enlightening,' at the moment of maximum vulnerability, triggering the final snapping of the protagonist's composure. Later, the board erupts into applause for a demonstrably flawed presentation, praising it as 'exactly the forward thinking we need.'	Unlike generic board members, this collective variant weaponizes corporate gaslighting through synchronized invalidation—asking irrelevant questions designed to undermine, maintaining silent judgment masking condescension, and then applauding visible failures as success. They are more dangerous than individual critics because their collective performance rewrites reality itself, forcing the protagonist to doubt their own perception of objective failure.	22	claude	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	2026-02-27 13:17:06.05021-05	2026-03-14 18:06:15.112419-04	2	\N
