420	The Bumbling COO	t	A manipulative figure who has wormed his way into the CEO's inner chambers through a lifelong 'affair,' weaponizing his proximity to power. His presence radiates incompetence and blame-shifting, with labored, oppressive breathing and a voice that cuts through consciousness like a sharp knife. He represents not raw power but parasitic toxicity that drains the protagonist's energy and feeds on workplace chaos.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Described as 'the bumbling COO who has somehow wormed his way into the CEO's inner chambers'; 'his promised innovations turning out to be nothing but impossible dreams'; 'his frustration with our lack of progress is straining his lifelong affair with the CEO'; 'his labored breathing grows louder and more oppressive'; 'each of his mistakes that I must answer for'; 'this parasite no longer deserved my energy.'	Bellows through the receiver: 'I need you in the office immediately to sort this mess out.' Later identified as a parasite whose voice becomes merely a distant hum as the protagonist reclaims their boundaries.	Unlike typical bosses, this COO's power derives not from competence or authority earned, but from exploiting personal relationships with the CEO while systematically blaming competent employees for failures created by his own incompetence. His greatest weapon is psychological manipulation and the institutional protection afforded by his affair with leadership, making him a persistent, inescapable threat to the protagonist's mental health and career.	25	claude	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	2026-02-27 13:24:09.210121-05	2026-03-14 18:06:15.112419-04	2	\N
