436	The Erasure	t	An unseen but systematically efficient entity capable of purging digital records and human memories with surgical precision. It leaves no forensic trace of its operation—only absence. The Erasure operates across multiple domains simultaneously (internet, local storage, human cognition), suggesting either distributed network intelligence or a singular force with omnipresent reach.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	The complete vanishing of all Pointer-related content: 'Every news article, social media post, and obscure conspiracy theory forum—all scrubbed clean from the internet.' Most crucially, Mattias's genuine inability to recall a conversation that happened 'not even an hour ago,' combined with his authentic confusion rather than evasion, suggests the Erasure is actively modifying neural pathways in real-time.	The Erasure's signature action is systematic deletion followed by enforced forgetting: 'How could he not remember? Was I losing it, or had something, or someone, made him forget? The alternative was far scarier: was I unexpectedly remembering something that wasn't really there?'	Unlike standard information suppression or conspiracy cover-ups, the Erasure demonstrates capabilities beyond technological censorship—it is rewriting human memory itself, making it fundamentally more dangerous than any conventional threat. It operates invisibly and leaves victims unable to even recognize they've been compromised. The Narrator is the only entity aware of the discrepancies, making him uniquely positioned to resist—or to be next.	26	claude	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	2026-02-27 13:46:56.316269-05	2026-03-14 18:06:15.112419-04	2	\N
