572	The Power of Infinity	t	A clearing alive with impossible geometry, manifesting as shadows of hidden gears and tendrils moving in defiance of logic. It exists in a liminal state—empty yet alive, not fully tangible nor intangible. An aura of hidden knowledge and glimpses of unmade futures surround it, demanding a price from those who witness it.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Described as 'a great and terrible thing, hidden deep within the forest'; 'an empty space, alive yet not alive'; scouts heard 'a relentless hum' resonating through trees and vibrating in their bones as they approached; those who saw it were 'never the same,' returning with 'hollow' eyes as if 'a piece of them had been left behind.'	The clearing 'whispered its name' to the scouts and offered 'glimpses of what could be—future paths, unspoken truths, choices that had yet to be made,' while demanding something in return.	Unlike ordinary forest locations, the Power of Infinity is a sentient, predatory force that transforms those who encounter it. It communicates through a relentless hum, lures explorers deeper, and extracts a metaphysical price—a hollow absence in the soul of survivors. Its existence exists beyond normal spatial logic, making it a focal point of narrative dread and the thematic center of the forest's testing power.	35	claude	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	2026-02-27 13:51:55.298684-05	2026-03-14 18:06:15.112419-04	2	\N
