598	The Vanished Patrol	t	A scout patrol of trained, prepared young people who have mysteriously disappeared in a seemingly normal forest during daylight navigation activities. Their absence is profound and unexplainable, contrasting sharply with all other successful groups returning to camp.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	The patrol 'never appears' despite 'weeks of training and planning'; scouts fail to reach 'several nearby checkpoints, not even the easiest ones.' Their disappearance is confirmed by the scoutmaster, triggering the narrator's 'worst fear.'	The scoutmaster confirmed my worst fear: my son's patrol was missing. Despite the weeks of training and planning, none of my son's patrol had reached several nearby checkpoints, not even the easiest ones.	Unlike standard missing persons scenarios, this patrol vanishes completely without evidence of mishap, accident, or communication. They leave no trace, no explanation, and represent an impossible gap in an otherwise normal day—marking a supernatural or incomprehensible threat greater than simple wilderness danger.	37	claude	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	2026-02-27 13:52:44.252541-05	2026-03-14 18:06:15.112419-04	2	\N
