651	The Unnamed Ancient	t	An ancient, predatory entity of immense power that looms beyond the veil of nightmare fog. It does not manifest in physical form but rather as an overwhelming psychic presence—patient, hungry, and drawing the protagonist inexorably forward through an invisible tether. Its mere awareness fills the air with palpable dread and existential wrongness. It waits beyond the veil with the patience of something that has existed since before time, a looming darkness at the heart of the nightmare forest.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	"Something ancient and predatory loomed beyond the veil, waiting. I could feel it. Every nerve screamed for me to turn back, but my body moved forward, drawn by an invisible tether to a place I could not name." The presence exerts invisible control and fills every nerve with screaming dread despite protagonist's desperate resistance.	Drawing protagonist inexorably forward through invisible tether; silent waiting beyond veil; filling the air with palpable dread that overrides conscious will.	Unlike typical mini-bosses, this entity is never directly confronted or seen—its power lies in invisible compulsion, psychic dominance, and the way it warps reality around the protagonist. It is more a force of nature than a creature, more ancient cosmic horror than typical fantasy antagonist. Its true nature remains unnamed and undefined, adding to its existential threat.	40	claude	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	2026-02-27 13:54:34.864627-05	2026-03-14 18:06:15.112419-04	2	\N
