662	The Sacred Circle's Guardian	t	An ancient, sentient manifestation of the forest's collective consciousness, embodied through the gnarled tree, twisted branches, and malevolent whispers. It appears as a suffocating presence that tightens reality itself around the protagonist, with an aura of oppressive force that threatens complete consumption and erasure.	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	The forest 'violently resists' the extraction attempt; branches twist into a 'cage'; the ground 'heaves like a living thing'; protagonist faces 'the malevolence lurking in this cursed place'; the forest 'erupts around me in an explosion of sound and light' as climax approaches; tree 'shudders as though in agony.'	The world around me tightened — branches twisting into a cage, the ground beneath me heaving like a living thing. With a desperate certainty: if I failed, I would die here. Not just die. I would be completely consumed, erased by the malevolence lurking in this cursed place.	Unlike typical forest or environmental hazards, this entity is uniquely sentient and psychologically assault-focused, transforming whispers into agonizing screams and creating contradictory sensations (icy heat). It poses existential erasure rather than mere physical death, making it far more dangerous than ordinary environmental resistance. The escalation from localized resistance to violent eruption demonstrates boss-level threat intensity.	41	claude	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	2026-02-27 13:55:25.624876-05	2026-03-14 18:06:15.112419-04	2	\N
