721	COO (Chaos Incarnate)	t	A grotesque monument to vanity and ego; presence that seems to drain the air from rooms. Allegedly made a pact with unnamed dark forces, thriving on disorder and destruction. Described with Lovecraftian imagery as 'imbecilic Azathoth made incarnate.'	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	'From the moment he waddled into the office, his influence cast a shadow that seemed to warp everything it touched.' 'Late at night...I could swear I heard sinister chanting echoing down empty halls, a sound too sharp, too cruel, to be human.' 'His presence seemed to drain the air from a room.'	'Every meeting became a theater of the absurd, with directives as incoherent as they were impossible.' COO's signature pattern: over-promising miracles while under-delivering wreckage; deflecting blame while stealing credit.	Unlike standard incompetent executives, this COO appears to have supernatural backing, orchestrates deliberate sabotage rather than accidental failure, and maintains unnatural bond with CEO. His influence extends beyond normal corporate dysfunction into metaphysical corruption; staff attribute his rise to dark pact rather than merit.	45	claude	claude-haiku-4-5-20251001	2026-02-27 13:57:58.322291-05	2026-03-14 18:06:15.112419-04	2	\N
