r colonizing some newly discovered planet. No, this was different—it held the key to my liberation and the potential doom of everyone else. A monstrosity beyond comprehension, capable of altering the very fabric of reality. I couldn’t tell if it was a blessing or a curse.\n\nA blink of the eye, and eons had passed. Night after night would all lead back to this point. All my blood, sweat, and living sacrifices finally paying off. The cause of this destructive storm would always be my malevolent words made flesh.\n\nAt the heart of it all, beat the Eternal Engine. Its name was birthed from the very depths of my subconscious, a marvel of engineering beyond anything the world would ever see. It was a complex device masquerading as an infinite energy source, tapping into the very essence of reality itself. It hummed with a gentle vibration, pulsating in perfect harmony with the rhythm of creation. Its gears and levers twisted and turned, orchestrating a symphony of perpetual motion that defied comprehension.\n\nThese engines would come to power swarms of nanites. Each of their limbs were each made up of individual clones of Matter Replicators, devices capable of transforming ambient energy into any substance imaginable. With each mandibular click, they could replicate enough food to end world hunger, create hyper-exotic materials to build space-spanning structures, or even generate medicine to cure the most debilitating diseases.\n\nWhile each nanite was impressive in its own right, their processing cores, known simply as the Infinitron, held the real magic. These devices tapped into the combined knowledge of all the infinite realms surrounding our own. The pulsing cores emitted waves of Akashic data that rippled through the fabric of the multi-verse, creating an invisible mesh network between dimensions. It was through these portals that one would be able to glimpse every insanity inducing wonder and horror—incomprehensibility.\n\nIn my blind pursuit, had I unleashed a 