at moment, the next moment, things would silence, as calm as never before.\n\nNight suddenly passed without a trace, and it’s then that I realized that the first rays of dawn were peeking through the cracks in my workshop, exhaustion washing over me like a tidal wave, my body succumbing to the toll of insomnia. With heavy eyelids, I collapsed onto a rough cot in the corner, finding comfort in the pulsing glow of the engine that seemed to watch over me.\n\nA dream within a dream consumed me, transporting me into a realm of unimaginable wonder and terror. Flashes of images of the engine come alive with a surge of unearthly power, their force unfolding like a cosmic flower before my eyes. In this otherworldly dimension, I witness the intricate dance between energy and matter, guided by an unseen conductor that beckoned me deeper into the heart of the universe itself.\n\nI was wracked with a sudden pain and jolted awake. Panic seizes me, and I frantically search my surroundings for any signs of danger. The barn remains silent and still, the only sound being my own ragged breaths. My respite is short lived, as I am soon interrupted by a low groan coming from the corner of the barn. My heart skips a beat, and I quickly scan the darkness for the source of the sound.\n\nLooking down at my arms, I see the scratches are now glowing with the soft hues of dawn, serving as tangible reminders of the sacrifices made. Each mark represents a moment of determination and strength etched into my skin like a map of memories. I throw open the doors and head out into the fresh dawn air.\n\nThe sun climbed higher, its golden rays stretching across the farm, warming the dew-kissed fields and illuminating the sleepy farmhouse. The Eternal Engine, my bridge between the waking world and the realm of dreams, was no longer just a project. It was a portal to a destiny that I could barely fathom. What did all this mean? I stare at the rolling fields and distant mountains and can’t help but wonder 