red me. The ancient trees rose impossibly high, their warped trunks tightening the oppressive canopy above. Their skeletal branches clawed at the bruised sky, a deep, shifting purple that threatened to collapse under its own weight. Shadows swirled and slithered around me, darting and recoiling as if alive, their movements mocking my every breath. The air was thick with decay, a sour, choking dampness that seemed to fill my lungs with rot.\n\nEach step forward felt like trudging through molasses, the ground beneath my feet sticky, soft, and treacherous. The underbrush whispered secrets I could not understand, their voices sharp and brittle, like shattering glass. The farther I walked, the more the forest changed—its trees twisted into grotesque faces, their mouths gaping in eternal, silent screams. My pulse thundered in my ears, drowning out all other sounds except for the faint, otherworldly hum pulling me forward.\n\nMy eyes caught a movement in the distance: distorted figures flickering through the thick fog, their forms bending and stretching unnaturally. The wind carried their whispers to me, incomprehensible yet filled with malice. I pressed my hands to my ears, but the voices slithered into my mind like worms, crawling through my thoughts, unraveling my resolve. Something ancient and predatory loomed beyond the veil, waiting. I could feel it. Every nerve screamed for me to turn back, but my body moved forward, drawn by an invisible tether to a place I could not name.	0	43	f	2026-02-27 11:52:34.313836-05	2026-02-27 13:54:34.864627-05	normal	\N
