’s fury reached a boiling point, I stood my ground, my deep voice rumbling with authority as it echoed through the warped dream world. “Stop!” I thundered, my words rippling and reverberating through the twisted landscape. “Your thirst for revenge will only lead to more pain and suffering. There is another way.”\n\nHe turned to face me, his eyes like fire as they locked onto mine. His fists clenched tightly at his sides, ready for another burst of violence. “Who the fuck are you?” he growled, his voice dripping with venom.\n\n“I am here to guide you,” I replied calmly, determined to break through the layers of rage clouding his mind. “There is a path towards healing and forgiveness, one that doesn’t involve causing harm.”\n\nHe bared his teeth in defiance, refusing to back down. “Your fucking words won’t sway me! My ex deserves every ounce of suffering she caused me!”\n\nI took a step closer, towering over him in his own dream world. “Listen to reason,” I pleaded. “The cycle of vengeance only perpetuates pain and misery. Consider breaking free from it and finding peace within yourself.”\n\nHis eyes narrowed in suspicion, but a flicker of doubt flashed across his face. “Why should I listen to you? What do you know about my pain?”\n\n“I have felt that same sting too,” I confessed, my voice filled with empathy. “But holding onto anger and seeking retribution will never bring true satisfaction. It only prolongs the agony.”\n\nOur intense gazes held each other in a tense standoff, an internal struggle between the urge for vengeance and the possibility of forgiveness.\n\n“You make it sound so easy, where the fuck do I even start,” he murmured, his tough exterior cracking slightly.\n\n“Start with not fighting literal alligators,” I suggested. “Maybe try therapy.”\n\nThe swamp shimmered, and his alligator form began to shrink. The stormy skies cleared, replaced by a tranquil pond. The Florida Man sat on a log, suddenly human, staring into the water. “I guess I’ve been taking things too far,” he admitted.\n\n“Welcome to the first step,” I said, handing him a metaphorical olive branch, because in dreams, why not?\n\nWhen I awoke, I was consumed by the need to know if I’d made a difference. A quick search confirmed it: the Florida Man headline was no longer involving an alligator wrestling incident... instead he’d been arrested for streaking through a golf course, covered in body paint, chasing his Ex yelling about forgiveness.\n\nProgress? Perhaps.	4	246	f	2026-02-27 12:04:55.335255-05	2026-02-27 20:18:12.934201-05	normal	\N
