efrain from submitting falsified results.\n\n“Great,” I said, slamming my hands on the workbench. “Another blacklist. We’re really making friends here.”\n\nMy son laughed nervously. “So...no saving the world?”\n\n“Not today,” I said, rubbing my temples.\n\nMy wife gave a wry smile. “At least we’re learning one thing, this thing might be too smart for its own good. Just like someone else I know...”\n\nWe powered down the Infinitron, and the hum faded into silence, leaving us staring at the darkened screen. There was a lesson buried in the chaos: if we wanted to use the Infinitron, we’d have to tread carefully, and secretly.\n\n“Well,” I said finally, standing up and stretching, “at least we didn’t cause thermonuclear devastation this time.”\n\nMy wife smirked, shaking her head. “Next time, let’s try not to get banned from saving the world, okay?”\n\n“Deal,” I said, grinning despite myself.	1	101	f	2026-02-27 11:55:50.031329-05	2026-02-27 14:51:40.884139-05	normal	\N
