t defied comprehension. Their roars vibrated through my very bones, but what chilled me more was the darkness beyond, a living chasm that beckoned with forbidden promises.\n\nIn the next instance, the outward force reversed, and the portal started dragging reality back in on itself.\n\nIn a frenzy, I hurled the demons into the portal, their screams swallowed by the roaring void. The atmosphere cracked as the portal’s pull became irresistible.\n\nI resisted being sucked toward the light, terror and maddening curiosity warring within me. But the force was too great. I crossed the threshold, fragments of memory twisted in my mind, snapping under the weight of cosmic truths. Whispers rose in the darkness, promising enlightenment at a cost too great to fathom. My mind unraveled. A ravenous hunger took hold, a desperate need to consume the horrors waiting within oblivion.	2	109	f	2026-02-27 11:56:27.36577-05	2026-02-27 14:58:39.396494-05	normal	\N
104	27	4	The Eldritch Confrontation	Beyond the portal, the protagonist encounters towering abominations in absolute oblivion. After a fierce exchange of defiance and contempt, the protagonist slays the crystalline-toothed creature and claims a fragment of knowledge, but at great cost.	Silence.\n\nOblivion felt like surrendering to a living void. When I passed through the portal, existence ceased to exist. Yet, I continued to be. Time pressed against me, dense with malice, its suffocating weight sucking out my lungs and rending me into its oppressive embrace. Shadows writhed and pulsed, their movements hypnotic and unnerving, like the flicker of dying stars caught in an eternal dance. Towering above me were the eldritch abominations, their grotesque forms defying logic, their eyes glimmering with a hunger that scraped at the edges of my mind.\n\nOne stepped forward. To gaze upon it would bring instant insanity, it was completely indescribable. To me, it appeared like a hulking mass of writhing tentacles and jagged, crystalline teeth that shimmered like fractured glass. Its voice dripped with contempt, resonating through the void like a thousand whispers layered atop one another. “You dare to defy the ዴሞጎርጎን།? I am. Everything. I am. You are nothing but a fleeting speck, insignificant and doomed.”\n\nMy legs threatened to buckle, the weight of dread clawing at my chest, but I held firm. “I may be mortal,” I spat, my voice steady despite the chaos raging in my mind, “but my will is stronger than anything you can comprehend. I’ve come to rip the truth from your twisted lies and see what you’ve hidden behind this godforsaken veil.”\n\nThe creature’s laughter cracked through the air like splintering glass, sharp and vile. Each note gnawed at my resolve, threatening to shatter it. “Foolish fucking insect,” it hissed, its voice dripping with disdain. “You think your pathetic defiance means anything here? You think you matter? I am eternal. You? Nothing but a fucking worthless scrap of flesh. I was before time. I am fucking time. I will be when the last star dies.”\n\n“Fuck you,” I snapped back, squaring my shoulders and meeting its gaze, the fire in my chest burning hotter. “Eternity isn’t unbreakable. Everything has its cracks. And I will find them.”\n\nThe air grew thick with malice as the shadows around the creature writhed, slithering and coiling like a nest of serpents. More abominations emerged, their forms twisted amalgamations of flesh, void, and bone. Another stepped forward, its body pulsating like diseased tissue, its voice a low snarl laced with cruel amusement. “Look at this fragile sack of shit. So full of conviction. So ready to throw yourself into the abyss. Tell us, ahyceg, what drives you? What pitiful, fleeting purpose drags you here?”\n\n“Knowledge,” I snarled, my voice unwavering. “Knowledge that will unravel the mysteries of your existence.”\n\nThe things hissed in unison, their voices like acid eating through steel. It wasn’t a sound; it was a force that rattled my teeth and carved jagged trails through my thoughts. “Knowledge,” they echoed, their tone mockery incarnate. “Oh, yes. She is a dangerous, and stupid little fucker. Knowledge has her power, yes—but her seduction always demands its price. And you, mortal, are far too brittle to pay.”\n\n“I’ll fucking pay it,” I growled, stepping forward, my every movement like wading through quicksand. The space around me grew even heavier, denser, as if trying to smother me. “Whatever the cost. Whatever it takes. Nothing, nothing, will stop me.”\n\nThe void fell silent, the creatures stilling as their grotesque forms fixed their searing eyes on me. I felt exposed, every nerve screaming under their scrutiny, as if they were peeling back my soul to inspect what lay beneath. The crystalline-toothed one leaned closer, its voice low and venomous, each word sinking into my soul like a dagger. “You’ll never get that, mortal. Even if it were the last thing you ever did. Do you