adness and suffering. Whispers faded into manic laughter as they bore witness to unspeakable horrors that mankind could never comprehend.\n\nDeath, insanity, and eternal damnation awaited those who dared to meddle with the unknown. And the eldritch entity continued to watch, for it knew that the consequences of humanity’s actions would bring about the end of all things.\n\nToying with powers beyond their understanding, the humans had caught the attention of a higher order. A shadowy figure stood as sentinel for this group, bearing witness to the family’s folly as they tampered with the Infinitron - a device born from madness and chance, capable of tearing apart the very information of existence.\n\nThe being watched with ancient curiosity as the humans’ minds twisted and turned under the influence of this cosmic power. Their experiments led to grotesque mutations and gruesome deaths, as flesh fused with metal and reality warped into impossible shapes. But little did the humans know, they were just pawns in a larger game played by beings whose motives and intentions were shrouded in mystery, even to these eldritch monstrosities. As the three whispered among themselves in their unknowable tongues, these formidable entities debated whether to intervene or simply watch as this foolish race destroyed themselves and their world with their insatiable thirst for knowledge.\n\nA fourth being slithered into the conversation, its voice dripping with malice and madness. “No more deliberation,” it hissed, cutting through the hushed whispers of the other entities. “The time for watching is over. We must intervene before all is consumed by chaos and death. What souls will we feed on if they turn them all away?”\n\nAnother dormant entity shook off its peaceful slumber, its ghostly form now pulsating with a frenzied urgency. “What do you suggest?” it demanded, a hint of fear creeping into its once serene tone.\n\n“The mortals have unleashed powers beyond their grasp,” the sixth voice sneered. “We shall drive them to madness and destruction, reveling in the chaos that ensues. Let them drown in their own hubris. Then we feast.”\n\n“But what of our own realms?” the seventh voice questioned, trembling with terror. “Will we not be risking our own existence by meddling in theirs?”\n\nThe eighth voice chuckled darkly. “Let us revel in their pain and suffering, their souls only become that more delectable” it declared, relishing the thought of unleashing cosmic horror before drinking the refined soul torment.\n\n“We will plunge them into an abyss of insanity and bloodshed,” the ninth voice cackled, its once tranquil demeanor now twisted with vicious glee.	1	126	f	2026-02-27 11:57:19.260857-05	2026-02-27 15:13:21.912298-05	normal	\N
