emed to involve offshore banking—we decided to set up anonymous accounts in Switzerland and the Cayman Islands. The move would be bold, perhaps reckless, but it should provide the privacy and infrastructure needed to manage our astronomical resources discreetly.\n\nWhile I worked through the logistics, a gnawing unease settled over me. Success was supposed to feel liberating, but with every safeguard we added, the walls seemed to close in tighter. The wealth, the experiments, the strange phone call—it all pointed to one undeniable truth: we were no longer just riding the wave of innovation; we were at war with the very forces we sought to outpace.	0	185	f	2026-02-27 12:01:35.555398-05	2026-02-27 19:20:25.637792-05	normal	\N
