lutionize global shipping?” I said. “Imagine—instant delivery from anywhere in the world. No delays, no logistics bottlenecks. We could completely change how goods are moved across the planet.”\n\n“Like Amazon on steroids!” My son said.\n\n“Exactly,” I said with a grin. “We could start with smaller-scale tests—internal operations, maybe private partnerships—then scale up when we’re ready.”\n\nMy wife nodded slowly, her gaze sharpening. “If we’re careful, it could work. But we need to stay under the radar. No flashy announcements, no drawing attention to ourselves.”\n\n“Agreed,” I said. “We’ll keep it quiet. For now, it’s just us, the robots, and the gateway.”	5	203	f	2026-02-27 12:02:17.241235-05	2026-02-27 19:39:52.734381-05	normal	\N
