l moved in unison, their eyes glassy, their faces expressionless. Aditi’s hand, though steady, raised her phone as if directed by an unseen hand, and she began to record.\n\nThe glow of sodium streetlights bathed the silent assembly in a sepia hue, casting long shadows that danced in time with the figures moving toward the same unknown destination. Aditi followed, her feet finding the rhythm of the crowd without question, her phone capturing every step.\n\nThe crowd converged near the train station, a labyrinth of tracks and platforms now eerily silent. The air buzzed faintly, as though alive with static, and Aditi’s pulse quickened in rhythm with the growing tension.\n\nIn perfect synchronization, the sleepwalkers stopped. As one, they raised their arms, pointing toward Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj International Airport. The motion was mechanical, deliberate, and impossibly unified. The entire scene was surreal, like a living tableau painted with the strokes of the uncanny.\n\nAditi’s phone trembled slightly in her hand, the lens capturing the sea of arms extended toward the same enigmatic point. There was no sound save for the distant hum of the city—a haunting silence that amplified the otherworldliness of the moment.\n\nThen, just as suddenly as it had begun, the spell broke. The crowd lowered their arms, their gazes unfocused as they turned to shuffle back the way they had come. Aditi’s hand dropped to her side, her phone still recording, but her steps mirrored the others as she returned home.	1	255	f	2026-02-27 12:05:37.735014-05	2026-02-27 20:25:51.408193-05	normal	\N
