r perfection.\n\nLady I’s form shimmered with an ever-shifting elegance, like moonlight on a stormy sea. Lady A’s presence was heavier, grounded, her eyes burning with a quiet intensity that pierced through the chaos.\n\nTogether, they radiated power that felt ancient and unyielding, a force that didn’t just exist in the Threshold but shaped it.\n\n“Enough,” Lady I said, her voice slicing through the cacophony like a blade. The entity screeched, its form collapsing in on itself, retreating into the void with a sound that resonated like tearing metal.\n\nLady A turned to me, her gaze steady. “You’ve walked further into the abyss than most, but you haven’t yet fallen. There is still time to understand. Ignore the warnings of the weaver again and we may not be here again.”\n\nI could only stare, every fiber of my being certain they were here to help. Not in the way mortals aid each other, but in the way that gravity keeps planets tethered. They were fundamental, a balance to the unraveling chaos.\n\nLady I stepped closer, her expression unreadable but not unkind. “You’ve torn the veil, mortal, and with it you’ve broken through the cage surrounding Etheris, the boundaries between worlds. The power you wield is not yours alone, and the debt must be paid.”\n\n“I didn’t know,” I whispered, my voice cracking. “I didn’t understand what I was doing.”\n\n“Understanding was never required,” Lady A replied, her voice firm but not cruel. “The act itself was enough. You’ve tied your world to forces you cannot yet comprehend. But you are not beyond hope, not yet.”\n\nThey reached for me, their hands impossibly steady. The touch was not physical but resonant, like a tuning fork striking the deepest parts of my soul. The crimson void shifted, folding in on itself, and I found myself in a new place: a serene, warped reflection of reality. The landscape was eerily calm, but the air buzzed with potential, like the moment before a lightning strike.\n\n“This is not salvation,” Lady I said