ting them. You will encounter beings both kind and cruel, and your task is to discern their intentions. Navigate their dreamscapes with grace and empathy.”\n\n“How will I know who to trust?” I asked, my voice steady but uncertain.\n\n“Trust your instincts,” she replied, her tone grave. “And never, ever let your guard down. Dreams can deceive, and even the purest facade may hide a darker truth. Remember what I’ve taught you: recognize danger and mask your presence when needed.”\n\nHer voice softened as she added, “But do not underestimate your own dreams. They hold untapped power.”\n\nConfusion flickered across my face. “What do you mean by that?”\n\nHer laughter echoed through the dreamscape, light and haunting. “Dreams are a gateway to transformation. Embrace them, they will reveal what the waking world cannot.”\n\nAfter what felt like eons of relentless practice and study, the transformation was complete. Lady A stood before me, her presence luminous, and bestowed upon me the name Aspolin—dreamwalker.\n\n“You have earned this title,” she said, her voice suffused with both pride and gravity. “It is not just a name but a duty—a reminder that you are a guardian of the dreamscape and a traveler of its boundless realms.”\n\nDuring the final rite, she inscribed a mark on my skin, a symbolic tattoo that pulsed faintly with her power. It was a seal of my commitment to the dreamscape, a tangible connection to the lessons and responsibilities I had undertaken.\n\nThe dreamscape now stretched before me as an infinite expanse of potential, its dangers, and wonders waiting to be explored. Though the challenges ahead were sure to be immense, I carried with me the wisdom of Lady A and the strength I had forged in the shadows.	5	236	f	2026-02-27 12:04:21.441383-05	2026-02-27 20:09:10.308532-05	normal	\N
