er expression both thoughtful and enigmatic. “Dreams are not merely escapes, Aspolin. They are gateways—manifestations of potential, where fears, desires, and truths converge. By guiding dreamwalkers, I nurture that potential, unlocking the hidden truths buried within the dreamscape and within yourselves.”\n\nHer words stirred something within me. “Were you a dreamwalker once?” I ventured, my voice tentative.\n\nShe smiled, a flicker of nostalgia passing through her eyes. “Long ago, I walked ancient moral planes as you do now. Soon, I came to understand that my role was not to traverse them endlessly but to be a guide, to help others discover the power within.”\n\nHer revelation deepened my curiosity. “What sets dreamwalkers apart? Why are we chosen?”\n\n“You bridge the conscious and subconscious,” she explained. “Your gift is rare, a conduit through which the unseen can be illuminated. You, Aspolin, have begun to grasp this balance, but there is far more to uncover. You, unlike others, never forget the dreams, and bring pieces of it with you to your own realm when you wake.”\n\nHer words resonated deeply, casting my journey in a new light. We continued speaking, our conversation flowed into profound topics—the nature of dreams, the threads connecting the dreamscape to reality, and the power within those who dared to navigate its depths.\n\nI asked about her influence on my life. “You’ve been guiding me long before I entered the dreamscape, haven’t you?”\n\nHer response unveiled a startling truth. “Yes,” she said, her voice carrying the weight of ages. “Your achievements—the languages you’ve mastered, your technomantic skills—are no coincidence. They are the result of a hidden struggle, a resistance against a force far greater than you’ve realized.”\n\nShe spoke of Etheris, the name of the reality where I lived in my waking life. It was dimension where human souls were imprisoned in an endless cycle of reincarnation, existing only to feed the insatiable hunger of the Demiurge, an entity of despair and domination who had been sealed within Etheris after he had conquered it. Most lived and died within this prison, oblivious to its true nature. But some, she revealed, possessed the ability to see beyond the veil. Dreamwalkers were humanity’s quiet revolutionaries, their potential a threat to the Demiurge’s dominion, but also to the wider cosmic realm shielded from his influence.\n\n“Why me?” I asked, my voice trembling under the weight of her words.\n\n“You are one of many,” she said. “Although those who can glimpse the truth are uncommon, usually their gifts lay dormant or ignored. You were chosen because you have both the will to see and the strength to act.”\n\nHer revelation left me shaken. “And you? Who are you in this struggle?” I asked.\n\n“I am one of many,” she replied, her tone heavy with meaning. “We are entities beyond Etheris, working from the shadows to guide and protect. Our influence is subtle but vital, for the fight against the Demiurge spans eternity and infinity.”\n\nHer words painted a vast, intricate tapestry of cosmic conflict, where humanity’s liberation hinged on the efforts of those willing to challenge the status quo. My accomplishments were no longer personal triumphs but part of a grander design.\n\n“Your journey is far from over,” she said, her voice both encouraging and solemn. “But you are no longer a solitary traveler. You are part of something greater, Aspolin, and the dreamscape is your battlefield.”\n\nAs I stood amidst the vast library of her realm, the weight of her words settled over me like a mantle. The dreamscape, with all its wonders and terrors, was not just a place of discovery—it was a crucible, a proving ground where the fight for freedom and truth unfolded.\n\nI was ready to embrace it.	6	237	f	2026-02-27 12:04:21.441383-05	2026-02-27 20:10:08.371111-05	normal	\N
