was to come.\n\nAt the head of the table was the manifestation himself. Much like Moses in the desert, I AM had appeared to the Pope in the flames of a burning brazier. He was a presence more felt than seen. The darkness around this being seemed to thrum with an otherworldly energy, its voice, when it finally came, resonating like a whisper from the void itself. Flanking them were others, their roles, and allegiances veiled, their intentions threaded with ambiguity. Among them was Todd, his face marked by frustration and the scars of his failed uprising. His crimson hat seemed almost garish in this somber place, but it served as a symbol of the rebellion he had ignited on the day the world saw S Corp’s space elevators unveiled.\n\nThe air crackled with a tension so thick it felt alive. The silence wasn’t just an absence of sound, it was the pregnant pause of a predator waiting to strike. When Pope Lucius Sixtus VI finally spoke, his voice trembled, not with fear, but with the righteous fury of a man pushed beyond his limits.\n\n“In the name of the Most Holy Lord of the Most High. My brothers and sisters in Christ,” he began, the words cutting through the silence like a blade, “we can no longer stand idly by while S Corp tightens its grip on our world and beyond. Their lust for power has damned more than a trillion souls will defile the souls of many more.”\n\nOne of the strange entities, a gaunt figure with eyes that burned like embers, leaned forward, his voice urgent. “We cannot fight this war with faith alone. Technology must become our weapon if we are to challenge them. S Corp’s reach extends to the stars, but we must meet them there.”\n\nTodd slammed his hand on the table, the sharp sound reverberating through the chamber. “Enough talk!” he growled. “Words and guns didn’t save the people who believed in me before. We’ve been rotting in jail for half a decade now. We need action. A show of force. Something that will shake their foundations and show the world the truth!”\n\nThe room fell silent as I AM shifted, their presence casting a palpable chill across the room. When they spoke, their voice was deep, resonant, and layered with a sinister echo that seemed to reverberate from the walls themselves. “Subtlety has failed us. S Corp has grown fat on the spoils of humanity’s desperation. The toxification of the souls cannot be permitted to continue. It is time to strike their heart and expose the rot within.”\n\nA low murmur rippled through the room as the weight of these words settled on those present. Pope Lucius Sixtus VI’s hands gripped the edge of the table, his knuckles pale. “If we do this,” he said, his voice heavy with the weight of moral conflict, “we must be prepared to face the consequences. For every shadow we cast, we must bring equal light to guide humanity forward.”\n\nTodd’s grin was sharp, almost feral. “Consequences mean nothing if we win. People will follow when they see S Corp flounder.”\n\n“And what of the price?” interjected another entity chimed in, his brow furrowed as he regarded Todd. “What happens if we lose more than we gain? Every soul that escapes will only weaken our power.”\n\nThe room was tense, the debate teetering on the edge of chaos. Then, I AM spoke again, their voice silencing the room. “There is no victory without sacrifice. If we falter, the stars themselves will become S Corp’s dominion, and souls of humanity beyond our grasp.”\n\nThe room descended into grim consensus. Strategies were whispered, alliances weighed, and plans forged. The Vatican’s ancient halls bore witness to a scheme that would tether faith, rebellion, and forbidden knowledge into a precarious coalition. Amidst the planning, a sense of unease lingered, growing like a shadow over the gathering.\n\nPope Lucius Sixtus VI stood, his face carved with both determination and doubt. “We tread a dangerous path, my friends. But if it means safeguarding the soul of humanity, we must take it. Let us pray that we do not become the very thing we seek to destroy. And may God have mercy on our souls.”\n\nHis statement filled the silence, the chamber seemed to darken, the flickering torchlight dimming against an unseen force. The oppressive atmosphere grew heavier, as if the very room bore witness to the gravity of their plans. The figures dispersed, their steps echoing ominously in the labyrinthine halls.\n\nBeneath the Vatican, the rebellion was made flesh, one that would pit humanity’s deepest fears and flaws against its greatest hopes. But as they plotted in the shadows, something ancient and unspeakable stirred. The consequences of their actions loomed, and with it, the thin holes veil separating the known from the abyss threatened to tear wide open.	0	288	f	2026-02-27 12:07:33.693376-05	2026-02-27 20:52:51.181884-05	normal	\N
280	70	2	The Guard's Betrayal and Sacrifice	A Swiss Guard stationed outside the secret chamber sends a desperate message to his family on an S Corp colony before being discovered and silently murdered. His final act of love becomes an act of futility as the message never reaches them and the consequences of the Vatican's conspiracy begin to unfold in bloodshed.	In the shadowed labyrinth beneath the Vatican, where ancient stone walls whispered of secrets too dark for daylight, a Swiss Guard stood like a silent sentinel. His polished halberd gleamed faintly in the dim light, a symbol of his sworn duty. Beneath his stoic exterior, turmoil churned, a storm of fear and love.\n\nHis mind wandered far from the cloaked figures gathered in the chamber before him. The decisions being made at the table, veiled threats and cryptic proclamations, held the power to shape worlds. For the guard, their consequences weren’t abstract; they were personal. His family lived on one of S Corp’s colonies, light-years away. The fate of his wife and children rested precariously on the choices of the shadowed figures mere feet from where he stood. He was a man torn between duty to an ancient institution and an aching need to protect those he loved.\n\nThe meeting ended with the scrape of chairs and the shuffle of robes. The conspirators melted into the shadows, leaving the chamber steeped in an oppressive silence. Seizing the fleeting moment, the guard pulled a small device from beneath his armor. His fingers trembled as he composed a desperate message, his heart pounding with each keystroke. The words were simple: Are you safe?\n\nAs the message vanished into the void of space, he waited, the seconds stretching into eternity. His breath became shallow, each exhalation thick with anticipation. But the response never came. Instead, a chill ran up his spine, a shadow moved where there should have been none.\n\nHe turned, too late. A figure loomed behind him, cloaked in darkness, radiating an air of unearthly authority. Before the guard could react, a gloved hand struck with lethal precision. The blade was silent, the attack merciless. Pain exploded in his chest, sharp and cold, and his vision blurred. He crumpled to the cold stone floor, his strength ebbing as crimson spread beneath him.\n\nThe figure crouched beside him, their face obscured, their voice a silent, guttural whisper. “No witnesses.”\n\nThe guard’s world dimmed; his thoughts consumed by a singular image, his family. He saw their smiles; the way his children’s laughter had once filled their home. His final act had been for them, casting his message like a lifeline across the stars. The irony was cruel: his attempt to protect them had sealed his fate.\n\nAs his consciousness slipped away, faint sounds reached him. The squelch of a blade meeting flesh. Heavy, wet thuds echoing in the chamber. He wasn’t the first to fall tonight, nor would he be the last.\n\nFar across the cosmos, a family unknowingly waited. The message he had sent, his last desperate act of love, would never arrive. They carried on, unaware of the dark machinations unfolding beneath one of the holiest places on Earth. They would never know the sacrifice he made or the shadowy forces that had extinguished his light. The void he left behind would linger, an absence felt in quiet moments, a loss they could never fully comprehend.	1	289	t	2026-02-27 12:07:33.693376-05	2026-02-27 20:53:43.897003-05	normal	\N
282	72	1	The War Room Strategy	In the opulent Elysium office high above Earth, the protagonist and their core advisors—Patrick, Gil, and TJ—grapple with escalating coordinated attacks on S Corp facilities worldwide. The discussion reveals an ideological conflict deeper than simple insurgency: religious extremists view S Corp as demonic, and conventional counterattacks risk losing the narrative.	Thinking back to the dreams that started it all, from the small farm workshop where the Eternal Engine first sprang to life, I could hardly believe where I stood now. It had been five years since the Space Elevators’ grand unveiling, those colossal towers that launched humanity into a new epoch of boundless possibilities. From my opulent office in Elysium, high above the Earth, I gazed out at the sprawling spires piercing the heavens.\n\nMy core advisors gathered around, each a critical piece of the empire we had built. Patrick stood tall and composed, his tone clipped as he outlined the latest developments. Gil, sharp-eyed and analytical, absorbed in every detail, ready to act.\n\n“Escalations continue in North Korea, Somalia, and Russia,” Patrick said, his voice even but edged with tension. “What began as protests near our facilities has turned violent. Their desperation is growing.”\n\nGil leaned forward. “What’s their endgame? Are we looking at coordinated efforts or isolated flare-ups?”\n\n“Coordinated, but loosely,” Patrick replied. “They’re testing us. So far, our non-lethal measures have held. Zero casualties on either side.”\n\nI nodded, my eyes fixed on the Earth far below. “Good. The moment we cross that line, we lose the narrative. Keep it clean.”\n\nDespite everything at our disposal, the situation, however, had escalated into an all-out war. Nations, once content with passive resistance, now unleashed coordinated, vicious assaults on our security forces, determined to push out S Corp’s global dominion by any means necessary.\n\n“This is no longer just skirmishes,” Patrick began, his tone grim as his gaze swept across the room. “The rebels are evolving, coordinating attacks on multiple fronts. Their intent is clear: try to overwhelm and confuse our defenses, cripple our systems, and try to destroy everything else…”\n\nGill rubbed his eyes. “They think they can topple the future with rocks and fire. What they don’t understand is that we’ve built something unbreakable. Infinite energy backed with a limitless network of infinite computational devices. Not to mention an inexhaustible army of robots being built by the Matter Replicators. Still, we can’t afford to underestimate them. Desperation makes people dangerous.”\n\nAcross the room, the holo-screen flickered to life, TJ’s holographic image materializing with his usual air of calculated calm. “We must acknowledge that this isn’t just a tactical battle,” he said, his analytical tone laced with concern. “This is ideological. We’re not simply fighting insurgents; we’re combating a fundamental rejection of S Corp’s vision for humanity. Like the crusades in the past, this has deep religious connotations. Both Christian and Islamic, even some Hindu extremists, have been using heavy spiritual imagery, painting as us the devil, in league with demons, and our technologies portals from hell.”\n\nThe nuance of his words settled over the room like a storm cloud. This wasn’t just about territory or cultural sovereignty; it was about belief.\n\n“Our objective remains clear,” Patrick said, his voice resolute. “Neutralize the threat while minimizing collateral damage. Our technology gives us the upper hand, but we need to adapt faster than they can.”\n\nGil interjected. “It’s not just about defense. There are innocent people caught in the crossfire, people we’ve sworn to protect. We need to show them we’re better than the heresy these terrorists peddle.”\n\nI nodded, my fingers steepled as I absorbed their arguments. “Then we escalate. Not with weapons, but with outreach. We must connect with local communities. Provide more aid. More opportunities. Education. Show them that S Corp isn’t here to dominate, it’s here to uplift.”\n\nTJ’s image flickered, his eyes narrowing. “You’re not wrong,” he conceded. “But goodwill hasn’t won any hearts in this war. In fact, it seems to have been doing the opposite. The rebels are heavily entrenched in the local media ecosphere and are able to spread misinformation faster than we can combat it, poisoning minds with lies about resource exploitation and government manipulation. We need to control the narrative, but without access to those channels, it’s going to be almost impossible to make any progress. It’s not like in the early days of S Corp when we controlled everything and could just lock everything down and keep communications controlled. This is what happens when anti-intellectualism runs amok. Free speech and do your own research crowd has distorted what people think is the truth.”\n\nGil’s lips curled into a wry smile. “A full-scale communication campaign,” he suggested. “Transparency. Highlight our successes. Show them how many lives we’ve improved. We drown their lies with undeniable truth.”\n\nPatrick’s brow furrowed. “But truth is never enough. These terrorists have belief, staunch denialism, and emotions behind their actions.”\n\n“Then we adapt,” TJ said sharply. “We dominate every battlefield, physical, ideological, digital, and spiritual. Crush their networks. Expose their leaders. If we leave any room for opposition, we risk everything.”\n\nTheir words coiled around me like thick smoke, creeping into every breath, every thought. This wasn’t just a battle of perspectives; it was a fight to keep from choking on the truth.\n\n“Can’t we just buy some of these folks out? Forge alliances with those who align with our goals. Local broadcasters, pastors and imams who need new books or something,” I said, my voice firm. “And for those who don’t... we leave no path to victory.”\n\nA message chimed on Patrick’s computer. “Fuck! The situation in Afghanistan just went to hell,” he began. “Intel confirms that a faction of the Taliban, backed by splinter groups and covert Russian support, is targeting our personnel and facilities.”\n\nThe words hit like a hammer. Our earlier strategy of offering independent groups and historically repressed religions, their own colonies on the remote moons and distant colony worlds, had brought an uneasy peace to Earth. Despite everything, it seemed some factions still chose violence over progress.\n\n“Most groups accepted the deal with open arms. It gave them an opportunity to start fresh, on their own terms, without interference or threat from the outside. Free to pursue their own things,” I said, my voice tight with frustration. “They left quietly, took the offer, and moved on. So why now?”\n\nPatrick’s jaw tightened. “People love playing the victim. Not everyone is going to be content to leave. Some stayed behind, bitter and vengeful, and now they’ve found allies willing to exploit that hatred. This isn’t random. It’s coordinated. Fuckers are given the world on the plate and they turn around and shit in your face, then complain they’re being oppressed because they’re not allowed to poop on you.”\n\nGil returned to the room, his movements brisk, a stack of reports in hand. “It get’s worse,” he said, dropping the papers onto the table with a heavy thud. “Hindustani extremists are targeting our supply centers and education centers. Blaming the destruction on S Corp at the same time. It’s calculated chaos.”\n\nPatrick skimmed the reports, his face darkening with every page. “This isn’t just retaliation,” he said, slamming a fist on the table. “They’re trying to dismantle us from within.”\n\nThe holographic image of TJ flickered on the screen, his analytical gaze scanning the room. “We need better fucking intelligence,” he said sharply. “This seems too coordinated to be chaos. They’ve got to be organizing, or have a deeper center of control somewhere. We need to know everything. Capabilities, leadership structures, alliances, everything. Understanding their network is key to shutting this down.”\n\nI nodded, my mind racing. “Partick and Gil, get your folks to prioritize intelligence gathering,” I said. “We need to know who’s pulling the strings, how they’re recruiting, and where their funding comes from. Every piece matters.”\n\n“What about their propaganda?” Gil pressed, frustration evident in his voice. “They’re spreading absolute bullshit—claiming we’re raping women and children, then holding satanic sacrifices with the aborted babies. It’s poisoning minds against us.”\n\nI sighed, pinching the bridge of my nose. “Yeah, because nothing says ‘credible threat’ like some half-baked, QAnon-tier fever dream.” I shook my head. “Doesn’t matter if it’s insane—people will believe it if it confirms their fears. We need a response before this spreads any further.”\n\n“So, what’s the plan?” Gil asked.\n\n“Get Becca and Andrew on it. They’re good at spinning this kind of thing back on them—make their lies obvious, turn the fearmongering into a joke before it catches fire.” I exhaled. “We have to hit this on all fronts, not just react. Control the narrative before they get to it first.”\n\nGil nodded. “And if that doesn’t work?”\n\nI glanced at the monitors, the endless stream of chaos unfolding in real time. “Then we do what we always do—push forward, stay steady, and let the truth outlast the bullshit.”\n\nGil huffed a dry laugh. “Optimistic.”\n\n“Nah,” I muttered, watching the madness spiral, “just fucking tired of willfully stupid people.”	0	291	f	2026-02-27 12:07:56.46975-05	2026-02-28 16:45:16.775552-05	normal	\N
