 now fixed upon me, their collective gaze like the barrel of a gun to my face.\n\n“Ladies and gentlemen, citizens of Earth, and pioneers of our fledgling off-world colonies,” I began, my voice steady, yet reverberating with the weight of the moment. “Today, April 21, 2025, marks a profound turning point in the human story, a day that will be etched in the annals of history as the moment we stepped beyond the limits of imagination and into a boundless future.”\n\nI paused, letting the words wash over the audience. The collective anticipation was palpable, a quiet testament to the enormity of what was about to unfold.\n\n“Early this morning, we unveiled to you not merely an engineering triumph, but a symbol of what humanity can achieve when guided by vision and united by purpose. The space elevators, these towering conduits to the stars, stand as monuments to our unyielding pursuit of progress, our refusal to be confined by gravity, and our determination to reach for the heavens.”\n\nI allowed a brief silence, then continued, my voice rising in intensity. “But these elevators are more than steel and innovation. They are gateways, combined with our advanced ERB network, gateways to exploration, to collaboration, and to a future where humanity’s reach is no longer shackled by distance or time. Through them, we bridge the divide between Earth and the cosmos, rendering the infinite vastness of space not a distant dream but a tangible reality, accessible to all.”\n\n“The path to this day was neither easy nor straightforward. It was paved with challenges that tested our resolve and triumphs, that ignited our hope. Together, we overcame obstacles that seemed insurmountable, driven by a singular vision: to unlock humanity’s potential, not just for the privileged few, but for every individual, every nation, and every generation to come.”\n\nWith deliberate emphasis, I shifted to the broader significance. “This is not merely a leap into the stars. It is a reaffirmation of our commitment to Earth, our first home. The same technology that now propels us skyward will revolutionize life here on the ground. It will spark a new era of environmental stewardship, global connectivity, and economic opportunity, ensuring that the benefits of these advancements ripple across every corner of our world.”\n\n“We have worked tirelessly with leaders from across the globe to ensure that this moment is not just a milestone for S Corp but a triumph for humanity. Agreements have been crafted, resources aligned, and strategies developed, not to divide, but to unite; not to dominate, but to elevate every nation to new heights of possibility.”\n\n“And now, I extend to you, the people of Earth, a call to action. This is your moment, our moment. This journey is not the triumph of a corporation, it is the triumph of humanity. It is a journey that asks each of us to dream bigger, to reach higher, and to embrace the unknown with courage and conviction.”\n\nThe world held its breath as I concluded. “Together, we will venture into uncharted territories, confront challenges we have yet to imagine, and seize opportunities that will redefine the very fabric of our existence. These elevators are more than a marvel of science, they are a promise. A promise that humanity’s greatest days are not behind us but ahead, waiting among the stars.”\n\nI raised my gaze, my voice firm but imbued with hope. “So let us rise, rise as one species with Elysium, united by our shared destiny. The universe awaits, and together, we shall meet it.”\n\nThe final beep of the cameras faded into the stillness of my office. Gradually, another sound began to seep into the room, a faint, distant rumble that grew steadily louder. I paused, my breath catching as I realized what it was. Applause. It was rising from the crowd gathered outside the tower, so many floors below, their collective enthusiasm a force unto itself.\n\nI stood from my desk, my wife, and son moving closer as the sound grew into a deafening roar. The floor seemed to hum faintly with the vibrations of their cheers, and I imagined the sea of faces below, tens of thousands strong, their energy radiating upward like an unstoppable wave.\n\nI walked toward the balcony overlooking the sprawling landscape beneath the S Corp’s Houston HQ Tower. The sight was breathtaking. A massive crowd stretched far beyond the plaza in front. Streets for miles seemed at a standstill, people cheering, their applause creating a thunderous symphony that resonated through the air. Even at this distance, the raw emotion was palpable, a shared celebration of possibility, of unity, of what this moment represented.\n\nIt wasn’t just those gathered below. Reports were coming in from across the globe, people gathered in public squares, on rooftops, and in living rooms, their applause echoing in unison. Screens illuminated faces in awe, and the cheers of billions joined the thunderous clamor outside. The sound felt like it was reverberating through the very fabric of the world, a heartbeat of collective hope.\n\nI glanced back at my wife and son, their expressions mirroring my own awe. My son’s eyes were wide, his grin infectious. “Dad... they’re cheering for you.”\n\n“No,” I said softly, my voice thick with emotion. “They’re cheering for all of us. For what this means. For the future we’ve dared to imagine.”\n\nMy wife stepped closer, her hand slipping into mine as we stood together, gazing out at the crowd. “You’ve given them something to believe in,” she said quietly, her voice steady with pride.\n\nAs the sound surged and swelled, I closed my eyes for a moment, letting it wash over me. The thunderous applause wasn’t just a celebration; it was a promise, a resounding affirmation that the world was ready to take this leap together.	0	280	f	2026-02-27 12:07:04.18291-05	2026-02-27 20:46:19.829014-05	normal	\N
272	68	2	The Attack	A group of armed extremists led by Todd and Stacey, opposing S Corp as oppressive, attempt a coordinated attack at the plaza below S Corp's headquarters. S Corp's advanced environmental shields activate instantly, neutralizing the threat without harm, and the attackers are arrested, leaving the crowd in awe of the technology's power.	**********\n\n1400 Smith Street, the towering heart of S Corp’s global operations, thrummed with a charged energy that defied description. Beneath its soaring glass façade, a crowd had gathered, their emotions a volatile cocktail of awe and unease. The space elevators, a symbol of humanity’s boundless potential, had cast the world into a state of wonder, but also into the shadow of deep divisions.\n\nThe crowd rippled with conflicting energies. Families gazed skyward, their faces lit with hope and curiosity, while others, grim-faced and clenched-jawed, seethed with anger. Among them stood Todd and Stacey, their crimson hats marking them as part of the growing faction that viewed S Corp as the enemy, a shadowy manipulator engineering humanity’s demise under the guise of progress.\n\nTodd’s grip tightened around the concealed Smith & Wesson inside his jacket, his knuckles pale against the dark fabric. His mind burned with the fervent rhetoric of his Red Hats’ cause, each word fueling the fire in his chest. To him, the space elevators weren’t marvels, they were monuments to control, symbols of betrayal, and proof of a future stolen by a corporate juggernaut cloaked in the guise of progress, and working against the only true master of this world: I AM.\n\nHis eyes darted across the crowd, seeking the perfect moment, the perfect spark to ignite the chaos. Sweat trickled down his spine, pooling in the small of his back, as adrenaline surged through his veins.\n\n“This is it,” he muttered to Stacey, his voice taut with conviction. “They think they’ve won. But we’ll show them.”\n\nStacey’s eyes flicked to him, her expression a volatile mix of loyalty and unease. She shifted closer, her voice barely above a whisper. “Stick to the plan, Todd. No hesitation. No second-guessing.”\n\nAround them, the plaza buzzed with a sea of faces, captivated by the massive monitors displaying the final words of S Corp’s broadcast. “The universe awaits, and together, we shall meet it.” The closing line lingered in the air, followed by a moment of stunned silence from the crowd, a silence Todd seized.\n\nWith a trembling hand, he pulled the weapon free and raised it skyward. The cold weight of the gun steadied his shaking resolve. The crowd froze, the lively chatter snuffed out in an instant. Gasps rippled outward like a shockwave as Todd’s voice tore through the quiet, raw with desperation and rage.\n\n“They’ve lied to us!” he bellowed, his tone unhinged and crackling with intensity. “S Corp isn’t our savior, it’s our oppressor working with the devil. They want to control you, to control everything! They especially want to kill us Christians.”\n\nThe words seemed to hang in the air, sharp as broken glass, cutting through the awe that had held the crowd in its grip just moments before. Todd’s finger twitched against the trigger, and then—crack!\n\nA gunshot shattered the stillness.\n\nChaos erupted. Screams rippled outward as the crowd surged in panic.\n\nBut just as quickly as the chaos began, the impossible happened.\n\nA shimmering field of light erupted from the ground, encasing Todd, Stacey, and the hundreds of others who had arrived armed to the teeth, their weapons, and bombs poised for destruction. The force-field crackled with energy, its translucent surface rippling in sync with a deep, mechanical hum. It moved with an almost otherworldly grace, isolating the would-be attackers from the rest of the crowd.\n\nFaint sounds, like muffled farts were the only evidence of the multitude of explosions from incendiary devices around the plaza. Unexploded bombs disintegrated instantly, reduced to nothing by the field’s relentless precision. Bullets fired inside dissolved into harmless sparks of light, as though the shield consumed violence itself.\n\nThe crowd froze, terror etched into their faces, until astonishment began to take hold. Whispers of disbelief rippled through the masses. S Corp’s environmental shields, innovations born from Patrick’s relentless security and military research, had activated with stunning speed and precision, neutralizing a deadly threat in less than a blink of an eye without spilling a single drop of blood.\n\nA heartbeat; absolute silence.\n\nThen, realization set in: they had just witnessed the impossible, a technology not just meant to just protect, but to completely preserve.\n\nTodd’s fury turned to panic as an unseen force wrenched from his grip his gun, clattering uselessly to the ground. “What the hell is this?” he screamed, pounding his fists against the unyielding barrier.\n\nWithin moments, sirens filled the air, their wailing growing louder as police vehicles descended on the scene. Robotic-looking officers in sleek, S Corp-designed armor emerged, their movements precise and unhurried. The terrorists found themselves immobilized, their weapons confiscated, and handcuffs clicking into place. Todd’s rage gave way to a hollow disbelief as he was forced into the back of a transport.\n\nStacey glared through the shimmering barrier at the crowd, her voice trembling with fury. “This isn’t over. You can’t stop what’s coming.”\n\nThe shields dissolved as swiftly as they had formed, leaving no trace except for the sense of awe and unease lingering in the air.\n\nAnother pulse; not a sound.\n\nThen, a ripple of applause began, hesitant at first, then swelling as the crowd processed what they had just witnessed.\n\nS Corp’s defenses had held. No one was harmed. Celebration resumed, but the undercurrent of unease remained.\n\nSitting in the back of the police vehicle, Todd’s mind shattered into a million pieces. Just moments ago, he had been a passionate revolutionary, ready to spark a rebellion against the oppressive forces that controlled society. Now, he was nothing more than a helpless captive in the back of a police transport, desperately attempting to understand the chaos that had consumed him.\n\nThe sudden shift from brave warrior to confused prisoner left Todd feeling as though he had woken up from a nightmare. But this was no dream. It was a harsh reality that the S Corp would be impossible to beat.	1	281	t	2026-02-27 12:07:04.18291-05	2026-02-27 20:47:15.516651-05	normal	\N
273	69	1	The Golden Ticket	Yukiko and her young brother Takashi prepare for an unprecedented journey as civilian colonists beyond the solar system. As they board the space elevator with their family, Yukiko reassures her anxious brother while an older passenger offers wisdom about cherishing shared moments.	Yukiko’s heart raced with a mix of excitement and anticipation, its rhythm matching the tempo of her thoughts. For as long as she could remember, the stars had whispered to her, their distant twinkling promising adventure and discovery beyond the limits of her imagination. And now, on the cusp of turning seven, she was about to embark on a journey that most could only ever dream of. With a stroke of luck, she had won a contest, securing a golden ticket for her family to be among the first civilian colonists to venture beyond the confines of the solar system. The technological marvels crafted by S Corp. made this extraordinary voyage possible\n\nHer little brother, Takashi, clung to her hand, his wide eyes reflecting a mixture of awe and apprehension. Though merely three years old, he couldn’t fully fathom the magnitude of their upcoming odyssey, but he sensed its extraordinary nature. Sensing his unease, Yukiko squeezed his hand reassuringly, embracing the role of the brave older sister, determined to show him that there was nothing to fear.\n\n“Nee-san,” Takashi whispered, his voice barely audible over the excited chatter around them. “Are there going to be aliens?”\n\nYukiko smiled affectionately at her little brother. “I don’t know, Taki-chan,” she replied, her own excitement bubbling in her voice. “But that’s what makes this journey so special. We’re going to discover things we’ve never even imagined, things that might seem like magic.”\n\nTakashi’s eyes widened even further, a mix of wonder and curiosity filling them. “Magic?” he repeated in awe.\n\nShe nodded, ruffling his hair gently. “Yes, magic in the form of stars and planets, and who knows what else? Maybe we’ll meet friendly creatures from other worlds or see breathtaking landscapes beyond our wildest dreams.”\n\nThe intercom crackled to life, interrupting their conversation. A soothing voice announced, “Ladies and gentlemen, we are preparing for departure. Please make your way to your cabins or find a seat on the external viewing deck.”\n\n“Dreams really do come true,” she murmured to herself.\n\nJust then, a fellow passenger seated nearby leaned over and caught Yukiko’s attention. The woman had kind eyes and a warm smile. “Hello,” she said softly. “I couldn’t help but overhear your conversation with your brother. It’s truly a magical journey we’re embarking on.”\n\nYukiko returned the smile gratefully. “It certainly is,” she replied. “I can’t believe we’re actually here.”\n\nThe woman nodded knowingly. “You’ll both have experiences that will shape you forever,” she said. “Remember to cherish every moment, especially those shared with loved ones.”\n\nYukiko glanced at Takashi, watching as he marveled at the space elevator’s interior. She felt a surge of gratitude for the opportunity to share this adventure with him and her family.\n\nWhen the elevator began its ascent, the passengers grabbed their arm rests and held their breath. Yukiko squeezed Takashi’s hand one more time, a silent promise passing between them. No matter what they encountered on this extraordinary journey, they would face it together, side by side.\n\nWith their eyes fixed on the vast expanse beyond, Yukiko whispered, “Hold on tight, Taki. Our adventure is about to begin.”	0	282	f	2026-02-27 12:07:22.391248-05	2026-02-27 20:48:32.244877-05	normal	\N
514	127	5	My Lai and the Crack in the Prison	Stephen recalls his incarnation as Hobart McComas III, a Vietnam-era marine who fell desperately in love with a Vietnamese woman and fathered twins with her, only for both to die in the My Lai massacre, creating the first major fracture in the prison.	"You met Mom," Xavier said.\n\n"I met your mother," I agreed. "And here's where it gets complicated. See, in every previous cycle, I was never allowed to have children. Never. The prison made sure of it. Kept me searching, kept me alone. Because if I ever settled down, ever stopped searching, the power source might destabilize."\n\n"But this time..." Maeve prompted.\n\n"This time, I met a woman who seemed perfect. Loving enough to make me stay, cold enough to keep me searching. A construct. An NPC designed to keep me docile." I looked at Xavier. "But somehow those safeguards were offline. So we had a son."\n\nXavier's face went pale. "Me."\n\n"You," I confirmed. "But you're not hers. Not really. You're..." I struggled for the words. "You're a spirit I pulled from somewhere. Deep through the dream plane, deep into the folds of Yaldabaoth himself. Without even knowing what I was doing. I reached into the void, into that pocket of anti-reality at the center where all the consumed souls were trapped, desperate for family, and I grabbed you. Pulled you across. Made you real in a place where you were never supposed to exist."\n\n"That's why I see the NPCs," Xavier whispered. "Why I can tell the difference."\n\n"Because you're not from here," I said. "You were never part of the prison's design. You're a foreign object. A glitch. And your existence..." I swallowed. "Your existence destabilized everything. Made the prison start to fracture in earnest."\n\nXavier was staring at me, trying to understand.\n\n"After you were born, the system tried to fix things," I continued. "But it created three resets. Three attempts to correct the error. In the first one, I suddenly had the power of a god. The Eternal Engine. I defeated Yaldabaoth completely. Tore him apart."\n\n"But that triggered a reset," Xavier said.\n\n"Exactly. In the second reset, I grew old and died naturally. But instead of being reincarnated like every other cycle, I triggered another reset. The system threw me back to high school and pulled Velistra into reality, incarnated her as Jamie. I found Yaldabaoth again, fought him again... and triggered this reset."\n\nI looked at him.\n\n"The one I'm just now remembering. The one where you exist. Where I met my wife and somehow had a son who was never supposed to be born."	4	528	f	2026-02-27 12:30:11.403392-05	2026-02-28 23:14:46.264854-05	normal	\N
531	130	3	Negotiation with the Crawling Chaos	Stephen summons Nyarlathotep and successfully negotiates passage through the barrier by appealing to the entity's boredom with the stagnant prison. The barrier opens, granting him access to the interior of the Pyramid.	No pressure.\n\nI raise my voice.\n\n"Nyarlathotep." The name makes my mouth tingle. "I need to pass. I need to go deeper."\n\nSilence.\n\nThen—laughter.\n\nNot from anywhere. Not from everywhere. Just... laughter. Cold. Amused. Ancient.\n\nThe shimmer resolves.\n\nHe's standing there. Has been the whole time. Wearing a suit that's too well-tailored for this place. His face is handsome. Human. But his eyes are wrong. Too many dimensions behind them.\n\n"You," he says, "are either very brave or very stupid."\n\n"Both," I manage. "Probably."\n\nHe smiles. It doesn't reach his eyes.\n\n"You got out. But you decided to come back. Now you want to disturb the power source. To wake what should stay sleeping. To steal the only thing that’s holding this place together." He takes a step closer. "Why should I allow that?"\n\n"Because," I say, "you're bored. Because this whole thing—Yaldabaoth, the prison, the loops—it's all predictable. Stagnant. And you hate stagnation."\n\nHis smile widens.\n\n"Smart mouse."\n\nHe gestures.\n\nThe barrier opens.\n\n"Go," he says. "Tear it all down. I'll enjoy watching the aftermath."\n\nI don't wait. I step through.\n\nAnd the world changes.\n\nThe crevasse behind me is gone. The horde is gone. Even the sound—the constant screaming, chittering, roaring—fades to silence.\n\nI'm inside now.\n\nInside the pyramid.\n\nAnd whatever comes next... there's no turning back.	2	545	f	2026-02-27 12:31:22.457664-05	2026-02-28 23:31:56.677308-05	normal	\N
