308	77	2	Confinement and the Arrival of Nameless	Todd awakens in a sterile prison cell, disoriented and broken. A mysterious figure called Nameless arrives with an offer of freedom in exchange for Todd's compliance with an unknown purpose.	He awoke like every other day in his ruined shell of existence, to the sterile glow of artificial light. The cell was a featureless cube, its metallic walls reflecting the cold, clinical glare. The sharp scent of disinfectant burned his nostrils, mingling with the pounding in his head. Disoriented, Todd struggled to piece together fragments of memory, the rally, the shield, the crushing emptiness that had followed. Alone in this cell, his only companion was the passing of eternity, in his own personal hell.\n\nHe screamed, but no one came.\n\n“I AM. I did all you asked and more. What more do you want?” He cried.\n\nHow long had he been here? Days? Weeks? Time had become a blur, a suffocating fog through which he could barely see.\n\nThe door hissed open, and a figure stepped inside, cloaked in shadows. The man’s presence was unsettling, his voice smooth yet devoid of warmth. “Call me Nameless,” he said, his tone as blank as the name itself. He exuded an air of authority that demanded attention, his words cutting through the haze clouding Todd’s mind.\n\n“You want freedom,” Nameless said, his gaze piercing. “Real freedom. Not the lies they feed you, not the false hope you’ve clung to. I can give it to you.”\n\nTodd’s throat tightened. He wanted to believe—needed to believe—but half a decade of betrayal had left his trust in tatters. He glared at Nameless, his voice raw. “What’s the catch?”\n\nThe cloaked figure’s lips curled into a faint smile. “There’s always a catch, Todd. Freedom comes with a price. But it’s a price you’ve already agreed to pay.”\n\nThe words pierced through Todd like hot pokers. He stared at the man, his mind racing. For years, he had fought, raged, and failed. But now, an ember of defiance flickered within him