309	77	3	The Vatican Revelation	Todd is transported to the Vatican crypts where he meets Pope Lucius Sixtus VI and mysterious entities. They reveal that S Corp is a mask concealing ancient forces opposed to I AM, and recruit Todd as their champion to lead a rebellion.	The crypts beneath the Vatican were a twisting maze of ancient stone, each corridor heavy with the weight of untold secrets. Candles flickered in alcoves, casting dancing shadows that seemed to breathe with the darkness. Todd followed Nameless, the man’s steps echoing softly in the damp air.\n\nAt last, they arrived at an imposing iron door, its surface etched with symbols that pierced Todd’s skin and demanded blood as a key. It groaned open to reveal a vast chamber illuminated by the soft glow of countless candles. Two figures waited within.\n\nPope Lucius Sixtus VI sat with quiet authority, his robes pooling around him like liquid marble. His face was etched with lines of age and responsibility, but his eyes burned with an unyielding fire. Beside him stood mysterious figures, cloaked in austere black, his gaze sharp and calculating, like the algorithms that had shaped the last vestiges of the holy roman empire.\n\nNameless gestured grandly toward Todd. “Gentlemen, your champion.”\n\nTodd’s breath caught as the suffocating presence of the moment invaded his lungs. This was no fevered dream of conspiracy forums. This was real. This was power.\n\nThe pope’s voice broke the silence, a resonant whisper that seemed to echo through the chamber. “Mr. Todd, we have been watching you. Within you burns a fire they cannot extinguish, a defiance that challenges the very fabric of their control.”\n\nTodd swallowed hard, his voice shaky. “They? Who’s ‘they’?”\n\nThe entity’s gaze gleamed like polished obsidian. “S Corp is merely the mask. Behind it lies something ancient, insidious, entities who have been fighting I AM since before the beginning.”\n\nThe name sent a jolt through Todd, triggering memories of the lake side massacre that had lead him down the cryptic holes , the forum threads and whispered conspiracies. He had been building his following, but thought I AM nothing more than an affectation of his own personal madness. Now, confronted with the truth, the pieces clicked into place. I AM was real. Somehow, he, Todd, was at the center of this battle. The master was calling his puppets home.\n\nPope Lucius Sixtus VI gestured to a display that shimmered to life, its glowing display illuminating a web of data streams and global influence. “S Corp’s reach is vast,” the pope said, his voice heavy with conviction. “It suffocates the world in a web of control, and prevents souls from reaching the divine glory that is IAM. But even the strongest webs have weak points.”\n\nTodd stared at the display, the enormity of what they were facing was etched in every glowing line. The solidity of their trust settled on him like a crown of thorns. “What’s my role in this?” he asked, his voice laced with uncertainty.\n\nThe entity stepped forward, a faint smile tugging at his lips. “You, Mr. Todd, will lead. Your voice has already sparked, will continue to be the spark that ignites rebellion. We will supply the resources, the infrastructure. But the masses need a face, a symbol of defiance. You will be their David against the Moabites.”\n\nTodd’s gaze lingered on the information, the magnitude of the task lost in his tired eyes. For years, he had been dismissed as a crackpot, a relic of a forgotten cause. But now, he stood on the precipice of something far greater—a chance to matter, to fight for a future worth saving.\n\n“What do I do first?” he asked, his voice steady despite the storm of doubt within.\n\nThe pope’s gaze softened, his voice resolute. “You light the fire. And we’ll show you how.”	2	321	t	2026-02-27 12:09:32.109022-05	2026-02-28 17:21:43.349713-05	normal	\N
310	77	4	Project Janus: The Final Preparation	Five years later, Todd oversees the construction and launch of Project Janus—cathedral-ships designed to attack S Corp's gateway on Pluto. With a diverse crew of Vatican scientists, engineers, and priests, he prepares for humanity's last stand against the forces of control.	It had been nearly five years of preparation since their first encounter with the Nameless. After emerging from the meeting with the remaining nine entities, he realized how entrenched S Corp was and how difficult everything was going to be to take them down. While he had worked on the outside, growing the influence of the Red Hats, the other 9 were already working in the shadows, taking down S Corps internals and causing as much chaos as they could to try an overwhelm everything. S Corp wouldn’t fall with brute force alone; it had to be dismantled piece by piece, infiltrated and undermined until its foundations collapsed.\n\nWhat Todd had built over the past 5 years since the failed attack on S Corp headquarters was more than rebellion. The Red Hats were merely the first ripples of a coming storm. And Todd, now the reluctant prophet of I AM, stood at its center, ready to lead the charge.\n\nBeneath vaulted ceilings adorned with celestial instruments and faded astrological charts, Project Janus hummed to life. The skeletal frames of the ships, half cathedral, half ark, gleamed under the cold illumination. These vessels, forged in secrecy and desperation, were more than just spacecraft; they were weapons of faith and defiance, designed to tear through the heart of S Corp’s Exo-stellar Expedition Center on Pluto.\n\nTodd stood on the command deck; his gaze fixed on the holographic map hovering before him. Pluto flickered at the edge of the display, a frozen wasteland pulsing like a malignant star. Through it’s gateways nestled within its icy expanse lay Sorhhinda. The massive gateway through which the powers behind S Corp must be siphoning their insidious energy. To destroy the portal and sever the link to Sorhhinda was to undo the tendrils of control choking Earth. This wasn’t just a mission, it was humanity’s, and God’s last stand.\n\nHe turned to the room, alive with tension and quiet purpose. Vatican scientists in their monk robes and wild, unkempt hair poured over data streams, their eyes feverish with determination. Engineers, their hands scarred from the fires of innovation, tested circuits and engines with obsessive precision. Priests murmured blessings over intricate machinery, their words a strange harmony against the hum of generators. The air crackled with a collective resolve, a desperate hope etched on every face.\n\nTodd spoke. “How long until launch?”\n\nAn engineer turned, grease smudged across her face, her eyes sharp. “Final calibrations are underway. We’ll be ready within the hour.”\n\n“And the payload?” he asked, his gaze shifting to a scientist hunched over a console.\n\n“Secured,” the scientist replied, not looking up. “If it works as intended, Sorhhinda will be severed from its source. But...”\n\n“But?” Todd pressed.\n\nThe scientist finally met his eyes, his voice heavy with unease. “It’s untested. If anything goes wrong, the resulting energy collapse could... well, we wouldn’t be alive to see it.”\n\nTodd nodded, the weight of the risk settling over him like a shroud. “That’s why we’re here. If we don’t take the chance, there won’t be a future to fight for.”\n\nThe room fell into a solemn silence, the gravity of their mission pressing down on everyone. Todd turned back to the map, his jaw tightening. “This isn’t just about Sorhhinda or Pluto. It’s about reclaiming what they’ve taken from us, our freedom, our agency, our connection of our souls to God. We can’t afford to fail.”\n\nA voice broke through the tension, clear and calm. It was a priest, his hands resting lightly on a glowing console. “Faith and science are not enemies,” he said softly. “They are tools. And today, they serve the same purpose: to confront the darkness.”\n\nTodd met the priest’s gaze, a flicker of gratitude crossing his face. “Let’s hope the light holds,” he said.\n\nThe countdown began, the observatory transforming into a flurry of activity. Todd moved through the room, offering steady nods and quiet words of encouragement. Every piece of the orchestra was in motion, the symphony of rebellion building to its crescendo.\n\nAt last, the ships powered to life, their skeletal forms humming with raw energy. Todd stepped aboard the lead vessel, his mind racing. This wasn’t just a journey to Pluto; it was a journey into the unknown, into the heart of a malevolent force that had shaped humanity’s suffering.\n\nThe engines roared, and the ship lifted into the void, Todd looked back one last time at the Earth, a fragile blue marble against the infinite black. His voice echoed over the comms, steady, and resolute.\n\n“This is for all of us. For the ones they silenced, the ones they broke. Today, we fight back.”	3	322	t	2026-02-27 12:09:32.109022-05	2026-02-28 17:22:26.798125-05	normal	\N
311	77	5	The Journey and Final Approach	Over months of travel powered by faith and prayer, Todd's fleet reaches Jupiter and prepares for the final jump to Pluto. The pope grants his blessing as Todd activates the Janus Gate to traverse the void.	Without advanced technologies, the fleet moved at a crawl, slowly traversing the solar system over a period of months. They would travel, pray, charge up the Janus gate and leap. Unlike the instantaneous portals to hell S Corp has, this was fueled by belief, the love of God and used heaven’s light to see it through. But it required a ton of daily devotions.\n\nAfter endless days of travel and countless masses celebrated on the consecrated altar inside, the fleet had finally arrived at Jupiter – meaning only one more jump to their target.\n\n“This is Todd. We have made the final approach and have entered the orbital lock within Jupiter. I am about to engage the final Janus gate jump sequence. I only hope that whatever the outcome, we can save the lord our God and execute all traitors against his will. Please pray for my soul. As I make, we begin the ultimate attack run against Pluto. Waiting for your confirmation.”\n\nAn hour later he received the reply.\n\n“My son, this is Pope Lucius Sixtus VI. May God grant you the blessings of wisdom, the strength of Michael, and may your retribution be swift and just. I am praying for your soul as you make the final Janus gate jump. Know that execution of the heretics will bring you blessings within his eternal kingdom. God speed and my Pluto be returned to the hell it crawled out from.”\n\nTodd exchanged a solemn nod with the papal envoy before activating the Janus Gate. Tendrils of light intertwined between the massive cathedral-ships, and with a deafening hum, a rift tore open in the fabric of reality. It revealed a shimmering maw leading to the frozen plains of Pluto.\n\nOne by one, the vessels, named for fallen heroes and inscribed with whispered prayers, plunged into the abyss. Todd stood aboard the lead flagship, the Galileo, feeling the ship shudder as it tore through the void. Stars blurred into streaks of light, the silence of the journey broken only by the steady hum of engines and the whispered calculations of the crew. Pluto emerged, a once desolate gem against the cosmic black, now defiled by the structures of S Corp. Their building’s jagged silhouette of the Exostellar Expedition Center loomed ahead, a scar upon the icy surface.	4	323	t	2026-02-27 12:09:32.109022-05	2026-02-28 17:23:30.331867-05	normal	\N
