of physics and challenged the essence of existence itself, each encounter pushing us to the limits of what we thought possible.\n\nWith every victory in the dreamscape, our spirits rose, while I AM’s influence faltered. The war remained far from over, but we had harnessed a powerful new weapon. Dream manipulation transformed us from soldiers into ethereal warriors, defenders not only of our empire but of reality itself.\n\nThe conflict stretched into an unrelenting stalemate, the Red Hats, bolstered by twisted necromancy, resurrected their fallen and corrupted our soldiers, spreading their influence like a malignant growth. Despite their relentless onslaught, we stood firm. The fight had evolved into an eternal battle across both the tangible and intangible realms—a testament to the resilience of will and the unyielding fight for freedom.	6	350	f	2026-02-27 12:11:27.804895-05	2026-02-28 17:49:15.053042-05	normal	\N
340	83	9	The Final Push Against I AM	The protagonist gathers his Oneiromancer squad beneath a skeletal tree in the dreamscape and addresses their exhaustion and doubt. He articulates the difference between fighting for conquest (I AM's goal) versus fighting for reality's survival (their purpose). He announces they will strike at I AM's core stronghold in the realm of nightmares, rallying the troops for a final offensive.	The moon hung heavy, an unblinking eye casting silver over the battlefield of shifting illusions. The air smelled of ozone and memory, thick with the residue of battles fought and lost. I gathered the squad beneath a skeletal tree, its twisted limbs reaching toward the void like the desperate hands of the fallen.\n\nThe glow of portable dream projectors flickered against their faces, half-lit by shifting colors that weren’t real—but then again, nothing in this realm truly was. They looked exhausted, shadows sunken into war-hardened expressions. Sleep was never an option when the war was fought inside it.\n\nI exhaled, rolling my shoulders. My voice had to cut through their weariness, carve into their resolve like a blade. “Another night, another battle against I AM,” I said, letting the words carry weight. “We may be tired. We may be battered. But we are not broken. Our empire’s destiny does not rest on wishful thinking—it rests on us. Here. Now.”\n\nMurmurs rippled through the squad—grit, steel, but beneath it, doubt.\n\nA soldier stepped forward, her face lined with the wear of too many nightmares. Her voice was sharp, challenging. “Commander, how the fuck do we fight something that doesn’t bleed?”\n\nThe fire in her words sparked something in the others. They weren’t questioning my command—they were questioning the nature of the war itself. A war waged in the abstract, where thought and will could be molded into weapons or chains.\n\nI locked eyes with her. “Power in dreams isn’t brute strength. It’s control. It’s adaptation.” My voice was steady