tion anymore—it's territorial. Final. Like they both know this moment will decide everything.\n\n"I'll go first," Becca announces, standing up to grab the bottle from TJ.\n\n"Actually," Jamie says smoothly, getting up faster, her hand shooting out to intercept Becca's with predatory speed, "I think we should let our gracious host decide." But she's already turning toward TJ with a smile that could melt steel or start wars, her fingers hovering dangerously close to the bottle in his grip.\n\nBecca's eyes flash with something murderous, but Jamie's already locked onto TJ like a heat-seeking missile.\n\nTJ glances between them, takes in Jamie's expectant expression and the way the temperature in the room seems to have dropped ten degrees, and makes the smart play. "Ladies first," he says with forced cheer, practically shoving the bottle into Jamie's waiting hands. "All yours."\n\n"Exactly what I was thinking," Jamie says.\n\nJamie places the bottle in the center of the coffee table with theatrical precision. The TV light catches the glass, throwing fragments of blue across the ceiling like broken promises.\n\n"Everyone ready?" Jamie asks, but she's looking only at me. Her eyes hold secrets and hunger and something that might be love or might be possession.\n\nBecca leans closer, her breath warm against my neck. "Ready as I'll ever be."\n\nThe bottle spins, glass catching light, reality bending around its rotation. It turns and turns, hypnotic and inevitable, while the basement holds its breath. Time stretches like taffy. The shadows gather closer, drawn by teenage desire and cosmic possibility.\n\nIt slows... slows... wobbles...\n\nStops pointing directly at me.\n\nMy heart hammers against my ribs like it's trying to escape. Jamie's already moving, rising to her knees with predatory grace, her eyes dark with triumph and want. Becca watches with barely concealed devastation, her hand still possessive on my leg, unwilling to surrender even now.\n\n"Well," Jamie whispers,