y," I gasp, tasting blood where I've bitten my tongue. My hands shake as I try to stand, fail, stay on my knees. "I... something's wrong. Something's really fucking wrong."\n\nEveryone's on their feet now, forming a loose circle around me like I'm some kind of exhibit. TJ hovers near his chair, Whitney holding onto her chest, Morgan and Patrick exchange worried glances. But it's the girls who matter right now.\n\nBecca kneels beside me, her earlier competition forgotten in the face of genuine concern. "Hey, are you okay? Do you need water or—"\n\n"Wait," I manage, holding up a trembling hand. Blood from my bitten tongue stains my lips. "I need to tell you something. All of you."\n\nJamie stands over us both, arms crossed, her expression a storm of worry and irritation. The kiss she was promised hangs between us like unfinished business. "Now? Seriously?" Her voice carries the edge of someone who's had their moment stolen. "Fucking universe couldn't have waited for like 30 seconds or something?"\n\nBecca shoots her a sharp look. "Jamie—"\n\n"What? I'm just saying, the timing's a little convenient." But there's uncertainty creeping into Jamie's voice as she takes my shaking hands, the way I can't seem to get my breathing under control.\n\n"It can't wait." My voice comes out stronger than I feel, cutting through the tension like a blade. "The dreams, the shadows, the word that keeps screaming in my head—there's more. There's something I haven't told you."\n\nBecca's hand hovers near my shoulder, not quite touching. "What kind of something?" Her voice is gentle, careful, like she's talking to some wounded animal.\n\nJamie's irritation melts away like ice in summer heat, replaced by something raw and protective. She drops to her knees beside me, her earlier frustration forgotten. "Hey," she whispers, her voice soft as silk, reaching out to gently touch my face. Her thumb brushes away a drop of blood from the corner of my mouth with infinite tenderness. "I'm sorry. We're 