d rerun of my worst memories," I AM gasps. The belt passes through me like smoke. The entity stumbles, confusion replacing rage. "Why... why can't I..."\n\n"Because you're not a god out here," I tell it, my voice carrying unexpected authority. "You're a rerun with bad ratings. A canceled show that doesn't know it's off the air."\n\nThe entity's golden light flickers, fading to amber, to brass, to dull newspaper yellow. "I am eternal," it whispers without conviction.\n\n"You were eternal. Past tense. Gods need believers. And I stopped believing in you… well I never did. "\n\nFor a moment, the thing that was Yaldabaoth seems to accept its fate, shoulders sagging with cosmic defeat. Then something snaps.\n\nThe rage that erupts isn't divine wrath—it's the tantrum of a spoiled child denied its favorite toy. The entity swells, golden light blazing back to nuclear intensity, cracks in reality spreading like spiderwebs around us.\n\n"NO!" it screams, the sound tearing holes in existence itself. "THIS ISN'T THE END! WE'LL GO BACK! BACK TO WHERE IT ALL STARTED!"\n\nThe void around us convulses. I feel the terrible pull of recursive time, the nauseating sensation of being dragged backward through every death, every reset, every moment of pain. The entity pours every last fragment of its power into one final reset, determined to drag us both back to the original loop, the first beating, the primal trauma that started this whole cycle.\n\nReality tears apart at the seams. The golden light becomes a supernova of desperate divinity, burning everything it touches. I AM reaches for me with hands made of collapsing starlight, its voice a hurricane of denial: "AGAIN! AGAIN! FOREVER AND AGAIN!"\n\nThen—explosion.\n\nNot sound, not light, but the fundamental concept of ending given physical form. The entity detonates like a dying star, its rage consuming itself in one final, futile gesture of defiance.\n\nAnd in the shattering silence that follows, in the void left behind by its tantrum, there is finally peace.\n\nNot violent darkness, but gentle absence. In the infinite quiet, I float like a leaf on still water, feeling nothing but gratitude for the nothingness.\n\nSomewhere distant, barely a whisper in the aftermath: "About fucking time, kid."\n\nThen only the perfect silence of a universe at peace with itself.	4	456	f	2026-02-27 12:20:35.047922-05	2026-02-28 19:31:56.652468-05	normal	\N
