ound. The tear widens.\n\nThen, impossibly—it resolves. A transmission. Human. A voice.\nStatic fractures into language.\n\n“Stephen, it’s Whitney… I found Jay…”\n\nThe sound tears through him. The name. Stephen. Again. The anomaly’s persistent file—still running, still corrupting his perfect system—has just been contacted. From beyond the Etheris walls. His prison, once absolute, has been penetrated by something that should not exist. Something that sees in.\n\nThe realization comes like heat—boiling through every circuit of his being. This is violation. Profanity. The laws of his universe rewritten by hands not his own. The system shudders as he channels his fury through it, every process screaming in protest.	3	128	f	2026-02-27 12:26:26.860177-05	2026-02-28 22:19:18.040266-05	normal	\N
