t the cold, oily slick of anti-reality rushing into my soul, filling the space where my love used to be. It seized that pure, desperate affection I held for my flock and twisted it. It didn't destroy the love; it weaponized it. It turned my need to protect into a bottomless, possessive hunger.\n\nI AM.\n\nI was no longer a shepherd. I was the engine of the parasite, a living battery of corrupted love powering a cage that would eventually swallow the stars.\n\nThe vision snapped shut.\n\nI gasped, stumbling back against the kitchen counter, my heart hammering a rhythm that didn't belong to a man who had just been drinking coffee. The smell of thyme and blood vanished, replaced by the stale air of the house. But the coldness remained in my gut—the echo of a hunger that wasn't mine.	2	487	t	2026-02-27 12:27:38.515738-05	2026-02-28 22:32:54.020373-05	normal	\N
