r.\n\nBecca: We didn't lol. Met by total chance at a Starbucks in '11. He had just gotten out of the Navy. 12 years!\n\nMe: James was in the Navy? Wasn’t he that guy who fell asleep standing up during a fire drill and had to be carried out by the janitor?\n\nBecca: People change! He’s all serious now. Dr. Henderson, actually. He got his PhD in, I kid you not, "Rhetorical Enforcement of Consensus Reality."\n\nMe: Wow. That is a looooong way from Atlas Shrugged. Remember that t-shirt he wore every other day? "Who is John Galt?"\n\nBecca: OMG yes. I burned that shirt. Literally. In a bonfire.\n\nMe: Doing the Lord's work. His PhD sounds expensive and useless though. Perfect for him.\n\nBecca: Haha shut up. We dated for like 9 years while he worked on his dissertation, before getting married. After that we opened a bookshop together over in Orlando. It's small but it's ours.\n\nBecca: [Sent a Location Pin]\n\nBecca: You should swing by if you're ever out this way. Seriously. We’d love to see you.\n\nI stared at the little red pin on the map. A bookshop.\n\nThe word triggered something violently different than the warm nostalgia from before.\n\nThe memory slammed into me—cold, vast, and terrifyingly ancient. I wasn't on my patio. I was standing in a cavernous space where the shelves didn't just go up to the ceiling; they went up forever, disappearing into a bruised, violet gloom. The air didn't smell like old paper; it smelled like living wisdom, dried blood, and dust that had fallen before humanity learned to speak. I felt small. Crushed by the weight of infinite, uncaring knowledge.\n\nThe Akashic Halls. The name surfaced from the dark water of my mind, heavy and cold.\n\nI blinked, gasping, and the clicking of the ceiling fan rushed back in. The crickets outside. The distant hum of the AC blowing.\n\nMy heart was hammering against my ribs, harder than it had when the glass shattered. That wasn't a normal memory. That was something else.\n\nMy phone buzzed again, pulling me back.\n\nBecca: Actually, you know what? You should come tomorrow if you can! We're having a little 'Five Year Anniversary' thing for the shop. Wine, cheese, James trying not to lecture people. It'd be great to see a friendly face.\n\nIt was a lifeline. A tangible, scheduled reason to leave this house, this loop.\n\nMe: Wine and cheese? I'm there.\n\nBecca: Yay! See you then!	6	490	t	2026-02-27 12:27:38.515738-05	2026-02-28 22:36:22.141398-05	normal	\N
