ht summoning rituals that cause your eyes to turn inside out."\n\nI looked at Jamie. She was smiling.\n\nChernobog gestured, and four symbols appeared above our heads. They didn't look like code. They looked ancient. Primal.\n\n"Etheris is back to normal reality now," Chernobog said. "And the cosmic seed is just a physical space contained within it. That means you won't be using admin privileges or hacks. You're going to be accessing your original divine powers. The ones you held in the time before time, before your reality was consumed by Yaldabaoth."\n\n"The ritual will allow you to tap into the fundamental essences of Etheris," Lady Illkeserod explained. "You'll have a direct line to the reality outside the prison to fuel your abilities inside it. It will take time and practice to re-acclimate—you haven't flexed these specific muscles in eons—but time is the one thing you'll have in abundance."\n\n"In the beginning, this is how they will manifest," Chernobog continued. "But where you go from there... who knows."\n\nHe pointed to my symbol. "Stephen. Lord of Wisdom, King of Life. Initially, it will be accelerated healing and flashes of intuition. But as you practice, you'll regain the ability to know what needs to be known."\n\nHe shifted his gaze to Jamie. "Jamie. Creativity and Death. You'll start by seeing the threads—the connections between souls. You'll be able to guide the awakening or ease the suffering of those ready to rest."\n\n"Xavier. Mischief, Chaos, and Laughter. You'll be able to bend probability. Find the cracks in physics. Keep things interesting."\n\nXavier grinned, testing the weight of the power in his mind. "Now we're talking."\n\nNyarlathotep gave Xavier a knowing glance from across the room. “You and I will need to talk about some things.”\n\n"And Hannah. Serenity and Joy. You are the anchor. When the chaos gets too loud, you provide the balance. The emotional gravity that holds the family—and the mission—together."\n\nHannah's symbol glowed