563	136	4	The Parasite Awakens	Kai's desperate act of power tears through reality itself, opening a gateway for the cosmic parasite imprisoned at the dead center of creation. The entity pours through the breach and merges with Kai, transforming him into something no longer human.	The ground beneath the creatures began to writhe. Roots erupted from the soil—not the gentle roots of spatch weed, but something else. Something older. Hungrier. They wrapped around chitinous limbs and squeezed.\n\nThe creatures shrieked. Tried to tear free.\n\nThe roots held.\n\nKai felt them. Felt every tendril. Every crushing grip. Felt the life draining from the swarm as the plants—his plants—fed.\n\nBut something was wrong.\n\nThe roots weren't just killing. They were changing. Growing teeth. Growing eyes. Growing things that roots shouldn't have.\n\nThe boundary between reality and anti-reality was thinning.\n\nAnd through that fraying membrane, something else was looking back. From its throne at the dead center of the cosmic seed prison, the parasite stirred. It had been waiting a thousand lifetimes, festering in impotent rage, starving for a way out. But now, it heard a key turning. It wasn't just watching anymore. It was answering the call to escape.\n\nKai gasped. Staggered. Blood was running from his nose. His vision doubled, tripled, fractured into a kaleidoscope of perspectives.\n\nHe could see himself from above. From below. From inside the roots that were no longer entirely roots.\n\nAnd he could feel it. The thing on the other side of the tear he'd just made. The thing that had been waiting in the impossible places where no life should exist.\n\nIt poured through.\n\nNot a clean surge. A seepage. An oily, living anti-reality that vomited itself into Sorhhinda's soil. A billion insects of nothingness. A tide of living absence.\n\nIt slithered across the broken greenhouse floor. Glistening. Iridescent. Black like the space between stars.\n\nAnd it struck Kai where he stood, his mouth still open in that scream of impossible rage.\n\nIt entered him.\n\nThe pain was absolute.\n\nEvery cell in his body inverting. Turning inside out. His spine arched backward, vertebrae popping with wet, organic sounds. His skin bubbled. Split. Reformed.\n\nThe last android stumbled backward, its optical sensors struggling to process what they were witnessing.\n\nKai's face… ran. Features melting like wax. His jaw unhinging with a terrible tearing of cartilage. His skull warped. Expanded. The scream of NO frozen in the reforming flesh, but its meaning… inverted.\n\nThe love for his plants—that pure, specific need to protect—wasn't erased.\n\nIt was hollowed out. Refilled. Twisted into something possessive. Bottomless. Hungry.	3	575	f	2026-02-27 12:33:14.303832-05	2026-03-01 00:57:08.979829-05	normal	\N
564	136	5	The New God Speaks	What remains of Kai stands transformed into a primal abomination, no longer nurturing but possessive and consumptive. It destroys the last android and declares its existence, spreading control across Sorhhinda's entire planet as warning sirens fade.	His body convulsed. Limbs elongated. Fingers split and branched. His flesh rippled with movement from within, as if a thousand things were crawling just beneath the surface.\n\nWhat rose from the dirt of that ruined garden was no longer Kai.\n\nIt was a primal, festering gash wearing the shadow of form. Eyes shattered like crystalline shards. Black. Reflecting Sorhhinda's three suns in impossible angles.\n\nIt saw the remaining spatch weed plants. The few that had survived. Still trembling. Still afraid.\n\nAnd for the first time, it wanted.\n\nNot to nurture. Not to protect.\n\nTo possess. To consume. To make them part of itself so they could never be taken again.\n\nThe android tried to run.\n\nThe thing that had been Kai was faster.\n\nRoots erupted from its body—not plant roots, but something else. Tendrils of flesh and anti-reality, wrapped in the stolen memory of chlorophyll and cellulose. They lashed out. Wrapped around the android's metal frame.\n\nAnd pulled.\n\nThe android came apart. Not destroyed. Unmade. Its components dissolving into constituent atoms, then into nothing at all.\n\nThe thing stood in the center of the ruined compound. Sorhhinda's three suns painted it in colors that shouldn't exist.\n\nIt opened what had been Kai's mouth.\n\nI AM.\n\nThe words came out layered. Multiple voices speaking as one. The voice of a gardener. The voice of something vast and ancient. The voice of love turned inside out.\n\nAround it, the garden began to change. The soil darkened. The surviving plants twisted, their stems thickening, their leaves sharpening into blades. They were no longer growing toward the light.\n\nThey were growing toward it. While spreading all across the surface of the planet.\n\nFeeding it. Sustaining it. Becoming part of the thing that now stood at the center of its own new creation.\n\nIn the distance, warning sirens began to wail. Then they flickered and faded as the root system spread over the entire planet.	4	578	f	2026-02-27 12:33:14.303832-05	2026-03-01 00:57:50.076814-05	normal	\N
