ty that my struggles are part of something greater. The rejections, the silence, the bizarre twists of fate—could they be the machinations of forces far beyond me? Am I merely a pawn in a cosmic game I can’t yet comprehend? The question haunts me, taunting me like a riddle I may never solve.\n\nRage simmered beneath the surface, threatening to boil over. How could someone with my credentials, my skills, be so utterly dismissed? Maybe it was me. Maybe I just sucked at life. Maybe the stories I told myself about resilience and adaptability were lies I used to cover the cracks.\n\nThat thought lingered, cold and unsettling. The whispers in my mind, the shadows in my dreams, the way reality itself seemed to bend around me—it all pointed to something deeper, something darker. Was I cursed? Or worse, was I unwittingly the architect of my own destruction? The question gnawed at my sanity.\n\nBecause if it wasn’t me... then what the hell was it?	5	70	f	2026-02-27 11:54:09.178259-05	2026-03-01 15:41:52.027098-05	normal	\N
