991	282	1	The protagonist reflects on five years since the Space Elevators' unveiling and surveys the current crisis with advisors.	Thinking back to the dreams that started it all, from the small farm workshop where the Eternal Engine first sprang to life, I could hardly believe where I stood now. It had been five years since the Space Elevators’ grand unveiling, those colossal towers that launched humanity into a new epoch of boundless possibilities. From my opulent office in Elysium, high above the Earth, I gazed out at the sprawling spires piercing the heavens.\n\nMy core advisors gathered around, each a critical piece of the empire we had built. Patrick stood tall and composed, his tone clipped as he outlined the latest developments. Gil, sharp-eyed and analytical, absorbed in every detail, ready to act.\n\n“Escalations continue in North Korea, Somalia, and Russia,” Patrick said, his voice even but edged with tension. “What began as protests near our facilities has turned violent. Their desperation is growing.”\n\nGil leaned forward. “What’s their endgame? Are we looking at coordinated efforts or isolated flare-ups?”\n\n“Coordinated, but loosely,” Patrick replied. “They’re testing us. So far, our non-lethal measures have held. Zero casualties on either side.”	0	\N	2	slow-burn	present	2026-02-27 12:07:56.46975-05	2026-02-27 12:07:56.46975-05	\N	\N	0	\N	\N
