r, exposed pipes, the usual unfinished basement stuff. But the walls… the walls were covered in books. Floor to ceiling. Stacked on homemade shelves, piled in corners, arranged in towers that defied gravity and common sense.\n\n"Jesus," I muttered.\n\n"Not down here, he's not." TJ walked to a cluttered desk in the corner and lit an old oil lamp. Warm light spread across the space. "Welcome to the heretic's library."\n\nXavier wandered to the nearest shelf, his eyes wide, tilting his head to read spines. "This is... insane. Are these... are these all real? The Gospel of Mary the Whore? The Apocryphon of Peter the Naked? The titles seem more AI slop than…"\n\n"They're as real as you are, kid," TJ said, his voice echoing slightly in the impossible space. "Welcome to the heretic's library. These are the books they burned. The ones they conveniently 'lost.' The kind of texts that ask the wrong questions and give the worst answers."\n\nHe turned from the desk to face me fully. His eyes were tired, but sharp. "Patrick called. Said to expect you. Said you were finally seeing the cracks in the facade."	1	\N	3	transitional	present	2026-02-27 12:29:23.081071-05	2026-02-27 12:29:23.081071-05	\N	\N	0	\N	\N
