1799	506	2	Stephen and Xavier discover Jamie's Marginalia bookstore has been burned down days ago, and Stephen realizes the system is erasing evidence of their presence.	It took twenty minutes to find the place again. We didn't need the GPS for the last block. We could smell it.\n\n"Jamie's Marginalia" was gone.\n\nIt was a shell of blackened brick and wet, pulped books. Yellow caution tape cordoned off the sidewalk. A fire department sign was stapled to a scorched piece of plywood.\n\nMy blood went cold. I got out of the car. The dates on the sign... it said the fire was... days ago.\n\n"No," I whispered. I'd been here. Right before this all went to hell. Right before I went to Patrick’s. It had been fine. It had been open.\n\nI looked at the ruin, and I understood. The system wasn't just chasing us. It was rewriting the past behind us. It was salting the earth. Sealing the exits.\n\n"Dad?" Xavier's voice was small.\n\n"Get in the car," I said, my voice flat. "We need to eat. And we need to think."	1	\N	4	contemplative	present	2026-02-27 12:29:45.517676-05	2026-02-27 12:29:45.517676-05	\N	\N	0	\N	\N
