You're tired of running from your old reality. The pain, the lies, the flesh that fails."\n\n"We offer an alternative," the woman purred, stepping closer. I could feel a strange heat radiating from her. "Why just escape? When you can have?"\n\nXavier took a step back, pressing against the wall. "Have what?"\n\n"Everything." The man gestured to the shadows behind him, where I could now see other, equally beautiful figures moving. "Sensation without boundaries. Pleasure that burns away the very idea of pain. We have seen what lies beyond the wall of sleep, and it is a banquet. You two... you have the scent. You are ready to feast."\n\nThey were like Cenobites, but instead of promising pain, they were promising ecstasy. It was the same trap, just different bait.\n\n"We just... we need to find someone," I said, trying to keep my voice steady. "We were told this might lead us to Nyarlathotep."\n\nThe man's perfect smile widened. "The Crawling Chaos? Oh, he is known to us. But he is a messenger. A servant. We... we commune with the King."\n\n"He is coming," the woman said, her eyes losing focus, rolling back slightly in ecstasy. "He will be here. And he will give you everything you seek. He will show you the way."\n\nShe took my hand. Her skin was hot and impossibly smooth. Xavier grabbed my arm. "Dad, don't."\n\n"It's okay," I said. "We need to see this through."\n\nThey led us through a set of double doors, into the main warehouse. The space was vast and cavernous. A makeshift stage of shipping palettes had been erected at one end. A dozen other cultists, all in identical yellow robes, all just as beautiful, were scattered around the room, some draped over broken machinery, others writhing slowly on the floor as if to silent music.	1	\N	4	slow-burn	present	2026-02-27 12:29:45.517676-05	2026-02-27 12:29:45.517676-05	\N	\N	0	\N	\N
