1886	532	1	Stephen enters the pyramid's interior and observes the impossibly configured hallway with ecstatically suffering worshippers of various species.	**********\n\nInside it feels like I’m being force fed honey and burnt wire.\n\nI stand in what might be a hallway. Or a room. The perspective keeps sliding away from me when I try to pin it down. The walls are too close and too far at the same time, covered in hieroglyphs that writhe when I'm not looking directly at them.\n\nAnd the people.\n\nThey line the walls like decorations. Dozens of them. Maybe hundreds. All naked. All in various states of... wrong.\n\nA woman hangs suspended by hooks through her shoulders. Her skin pulls taut around the metal, blood running in thin rivulets down her chest and stomach. But she's not screaming. She's smiling. Eyes half-closed. Breathing slow and deep. Her lips move in a whisper I can't quite hear.\n\nNext to her, a man kneels with his arms stretched above his head, wrists bound to an iron ring in the wall. His back is a lattice of cuts, precise and symbolic. Fresh blood wells from each line. He sways slightly, humming.\n\nThey're not prisoners.\n\nThey're worshippers.\n\nThe light here is wrong too. Not torches. Not electricity. Just a diffuse, amber glow that seems to seep from the stone itself. It casts everything in shades of brown, yellow, orange. Desert colors. But underneath, shadows pool deeper than they should, purple and hungry.\n\n"Enjoying the decor?"\n\nNyarlathotep appears beside me. Not walking. Just there. He's still wearing the suit, but now it's a different color. Was it gray before? It's yellow now. Canary yellow. Rustic red. Too bright for this place.\n\n"They chose this," he says, gesturing to the worshippers. "Every single one. I offer them clarity. Purpose. A way to feel something real in a reality that's all lies and loops. And they say yes. They always say yes."\n\nI keep my hand on the Mi-Go spine. It feels solid. Real. Everything else here feels 