ht in a breeze that isn't there. Particles of light and matter drifting apart. Returning to the fundamental substrate from which all things come.\n\nWithout his divinity, without his power, without anything to hold him together... he's just unmaking. Naturally. Inevitably.\n\nJamie kneels beside us. Her hands cup something I can't quite see. A light. A spark. The core of what made Sam who he was before the infection. Before the parasite. Before the choice that damned him.\n\n"I've got you," she says softly. "You're not alone."\n\nSam tries to smile. Almost manages it.\n\n"My flock," he breathes. "Tell them I'm sorry. Tell them I..."\n\nBut there's nothing left to say. Nothing left to tell.\n\nHis body finishes dissolving. The last particles drift away like snow in reverse. All that remains is the spark in Jamie's hands. Small. Fragile. Pure.\n\nShe cradles it against her chest. Protecting it. Keeping it safe until we can get it out of this prison. Out into real reality where it can finally rest.\n\nThe black mass near the throne gives one final shriek. Then falls silent.\n\nThe ritual is complete.\n\n**********	2	\N	5	dialogue-heavy	present	2026-02-27 12:32:28.849865-05	2026-02-27 12:32:28.849865-05	\N	\N	0	\N	\N
