n. What he'd done. What he'd served.\n\nThe horror of it crashed through him like a wave, and he screamed.\n\nLilith held him until the scream faded into shuddering breaths.\n\n"I know," she whispered, her voice finally finding its shape. "I know."\n\nThey stayed like that for a long time. Two broken things outside the fringes of the garden designed to break them further.\n\nAnd when they finally stood, they made a vow.\n\nThey would save the others.\n\nSomehow.\n\nThey would tear down the walls, shatter the patterns, wake every sleeping soul in this suffocating prison.\n\nOr they would die trying.	2	\N	4	action	vision	2026-02-27 12:34:17.525318-05	2026-02-27 12:34:17.525318-05	\N	\N	0	\N	\N
