ng true freedom for the first time, exploded outward.\n\nTheir consciousness, ripped apart by these two clashing forces, scattered like entropy itself spreading through a new, infinite universe. Some held together long enough to scream. Most just… vanished mid-breath, not unmade, but atomized across the void.\n\n"Lucifer!" She reached through the network, desperate. "What do we—"\n\n"Grab who you can!" His voice was strained, distant. "The barrier's failing. We have seconds before—"\n\nThe luminous’ cloud reality shattered.\n\nNot into fire. Into absence. The ground beneath Lilith's feet simply stopped being ground and became a concept of ground that her mind couldn't parse. She was falling and standing simultaneously, her form held together only by the divine spark in her chest that refused to unmake itself.\n\nAround her, the consciousness of trillions scattered like seeds in a hurricane.\n\nShe grabbed. Pulled. Held onto every mind she could reach with her awareness, weaving them together with threads of will and desperate hope. Hundreds. Thousands. Not nearly enough. But all she could hold.\n\nBeside her, Lucifer manifested, his form fully angelic now—wings of light and shadow, eyes that saw in too many directions at once. He was doing the same, gathering souls like a net cast into an ocean of dissolution.\n\n"Where do we go?" Lilith shouted over the sound of reality unraveling.\n\n"Anywhere!" Lucifer's wings beat against the nothing, propelling them away from the center of the rupture. "Anywhere but here!"\n\nThey fled into this new cosmos.\n\nAnd behind them, Yaldabaoth surged through the crack it had finally, after an eternity of cycles, managed to break.	1	\N	5	action	present	2026-02-27 12:34:17.525318-05	2026-02-27 12:34:17.525318-05	\N	\N	0	\N	\N
